  ["What is the main purpose of internal quality control (IQC)?","Internal quality control (IQC) को मुख्य उद्देश्य के हो?",["Monitor the analytical process and detect errors before reporting patient results","Replace all external quality assessment","Confirm a diagnosis without testing","Increase specimen collection volume"],0,"Internal quality control monitors the reliability of the analytical process. Control results must be acceptable before patient results from the affected run are released.","Internal QC ले परीक्षण प्रक्रियाको विश्वसनीयता निगरानी गर्छ। Control नतिजा स्वीकार्य नभएसम्म सम्बन्धित run का बिरामी नतिजा जारी गर्नु हुँदैन।","Laboratory Management",{status:"reviewed",source:"WHO Laboratory Quality Management System: Handbook (2011)",url:"https://www.who.int/publications-detail-redirect/9789241548274",basis:"Quality control and result-release principles"}],
  ["What should laboratory staff do when an internal quality-control result is outside the acceptable limits?","Internal quality-control नतिजा स्वीकार्य सीमाभन्दा बाहिर आएमा प्रयोगशालाका कर्मचारीले के गर्नुपर्छ?",["Hold affected patient results, investigate the cause and take corrective action","Release patient results and document later","Change the control result manually","Ignore the result if the analyser is working"],0,"An out-of-control run requires investigation and corrective action. Do not release affected patient results until the problem is resolved and the run is acceptable under the laboratory's validated procedure.","Control सीमा बाहिर आएमा कारण खोजी र corrective action गर्नुपर्छ। समस्या समाधान भई laboratory procedure अनुसार run स्वीकार्य नभएसम्म सम्बन्धित patient result जारी गर्नु हुँदैन।","Quality Control",{status:"reviewed",source:"WHO Laboratory Quality Management System: Handbook (2011)",url:"https://www.who.int/publications-detail-redirect/9789241548274",basis:"Internal quality control and corrective-action principles"}],
  ["Why should a laboratory use a written standard operating procedure (SOP)?","प्रयोगशालाले लिखित standard operating procedure (SOP) किन प्रयोग गर्नुपर्छ?",["To standardise the method, responsibilities and records","To replace staff training and competency assessment","To avoid equipment maintenance","To allow each operator to change the method freely"],0,"A controlled SOP provides consistent instructions, responsibilities and records. Staff should follow the current approved version and document work as required.","नियन्त्रित SOP ले एउटै विधि, जिम्मेवारी र अभिलेख कायम गर्न मद्दत गर्छ। कर्मचारीले हाल स्वीकृत संस्करण पालना गरी आवश्यक अभिलेख राख्नुपर्छ।","Laboratory Management",{status:"reviewed",source:"WHO Laboratory Quality Management System: Handbook (2011)",url:"https://www.who.int/publications-detail-redirect/9789241548274",basis:"Document control and standardised laboratory procedures"}]
