 // Clinical Biochemistry: liver profile, proteins, electrolytes and lipid profile; source reviewed.
 const biochemistryReviewedBatch2=[
  ["Which statement best describes conjugated (direct) bilirubin?","Conjugated (direct) bilirubin को सही वर्णन कुन हो?",["It is water-soluble after conjugation in the liver","It is produced only in the kidneys","It is always bound tightly to albumin and cannot enter urine","It is a pancreatic enzyme"],0,"The liver conjugates bilirubin, making it water-soluble so it can be excreted into bile. Conjugated bilirubin may appear in urine when its level in blood is elevated.","कलेजोले bilirubin लाई conjugate गरेपछि यो पानीमा घुलनशील हुन्छ र bile मार्फत बाहिर निस्कन्छ। रगतमा conjugated bilirubin बढेमा पिसाबमा पनि देखिन सक्छ।","Clinical Biochemistry",{status:"reviewed",source:"MedlinePlus — Bilirubin Blood Test",url:"https://medlineplus.gov/lab-tests/bilirubin-blood-test/",basis:"Bilirubin processing, liver excretion and causes of raised bilirubin"}],
  ["Which plasma protein is the major contributor to colloid oncotic pressure?","Colloid oncotic pressure कायम राख्न सबैभन्दा ठूलो योगदान दिने plasma protein कुन हो?",["Albumin","Fibrinogen","Immunoglobulin E","Haemoglobin"],0,"Albumin is the most abundant plasma protein and is the main contributor to plasma colloid oncotic pressure. It is synthesised by the liver.","Albumin सबैभन्दा धेरै पाइने plasma protein हो र plasma colloid oncotic pressure कायम राख्न मुख्य भूमिका खेल्छ। यो कलेजोमा निर्माण हुन्छ।","Clinical Biochemistry",{status:"reviewed",source:"MedlinePlus — Liver Function Tests",url:"https://medlineplus.gov/lab-tests/liver-function-tests/",basis:"Albumin as a liver-produced blood protein"}],
  ["A raised ALP result may be associated with disease involving which two systems?","ALP बढेको नतिजा कुन दुई प्रणालीको रोगसँग सम्बन्धित हुन सक्छ?",["Hepatobiliary system and bone","Lung and brain only","Thyroid and pancreas only","Skin and skeletal muscle only"],0,"Alkaline phosphatase is present in several tissues, especially liver/bile ducts and bone. Interpret an elevated ALP with other tests and clinical findings; GGT can help assess a hepatobiliary source.","Alkaline phosphatase कलेजो/bile duct र हड्डी लगायतका tissue मा पाइन्छ। ALP बढ्दा अन्य test र clinical अवस्थासँग व्याख्या गर्नुपर्छ; GGT ले hepatobiliary स्रोत छुट्याउन सहयोग गर्न सक्छ।","Clinical Biochemistry",{status:"reviewed",source:"MedlinePlus — Liver Function Tests",url:"https://medlineplus.gov/lab-tests/liver-function-tests/",basis:"ALP included in liver panels; interpret with related enzymes"}],
  ["Which electrolyte is the major intracellular cation?","कोषभित्रको प्रमुख cation कुन electrolyte हो?",["Potassium","Sodium","Chloride","Bicarbonate"],0,"Potassium is the major intracellular cation, while sodium is the major extracellular cation. Both are important for nerve and muscle function.","Potassium कोषभित्रको प्रमुख cation हो भने sodium कोषबाहिरको प्रमुख cation हो। दुवै स्नायु र मांसपेशीको कार्यका लागि महत्त्वपूर्ण छन्।","Clinical Biochemistry",{status:"reviewed",source:"MedlinePlus — Potassium Blood Test",url:"https://medlineplus.gov/lab-tests/potassium-blood-test/",basis:"Most body potassium is inside cells; serum potassium testing"}],
  ["A visibly haemolysed serum sample may cause a falsely increased potassium result because:","Hemolysis भएको serum नमुनामा potassium झूटो बढ्न सक्ने कारण के हो?",["Potassium is released from damaged blood cells","The liver produces extra potassium in the tube","Sodium is converted into potassium","Albumin binds all potassium"],0,"Red-cell damage releases intracellular potassium into serum or plasma and can cause pseudohyperkalaemia. Assess specimen quality and follow the laboratory's rejection or comment policy.","RBC फुट्दा कोषभित्रको potassium नमुनामा निस्कन्छ र pseudohyperkalaemia हुन सक्छ। नमुनाको गुणस्तर जाँचेर laboratory को rejection वा comment policy पालना गर्नुपर्छ।","Clinical Biochemistry",{status:"reviewed",source:"MedlinePlus — Potassium Blood Test",url:"https://medlineplus.gov/lab-tests/potassium-blood-test/",basis:"Potassium testing and factors that can affect blood potassium results"}],
  ["Which lipoprotein is commonly called 'good cholesterol' because it participates in reverse cholesterol transport?","Reverse cholesterol transport मा भूमिका हुने भएकाले कुन lipoprotein लाई 'good cholesterol' भनिन्छ?",["HDL","LDL","VLDL","Chylomicron"],0,"HDL participates in reverse cholesterol transport, carrying cholesterol from peripheral tissues toward the liver. The label 'good cholesterol' is a simplified teaching term; cardiovascular risk depends on the full clinical picture.","HDL ले peripheral tissue बाट cholesterol कलेजोतर्फ लैजाने reverse cholesterol transport मा भूमिका खेल्छ। 'Good cholesterol' सरल शिक्षण शब्द हो; हृदयसम्बन्धी जोखिम समग्र अवस्थाबाट मूल्याङ्कन हुन्छ।","Clinical Biochemistry",{status:"reviewed",source:"MedlinePlus — HDL: The Good Cholesterol",url:"https://medlineplus.gov/hdlthegoodcholesterol.html",basis:"HDL carries cholesterol from other body parts back to the liver"}]
 ];
 Q.push(...biochemistryReviewedBatch2); practiceQ.push(...biochemistryReviewedBatch2); mockQ.push(...biochemistryReviewedBatch2);
 // Clinical Biochemistry: renal function and acid-base balance; source reviewed.
 const biochemistryReviewedBatch3=[
  ["Blood urea nitrogen (BUN) is formed mainly during the breakdown of:","Blood urea nitrogen (BUN) मुख्यतया कुन पदार्थको विघटन हुँदा बन्छ?",["Proteins","Glucose","Fatty acids","Nucleic acids"],0,"Urea is formed when the body breaks down proteins and is carried in blood before being removed by the kidneys. BUN measures the nitrogen portion of urea.","शरीरमा protein विघटन हुँदा urea बन्छ। यो रगत हुँदै मिर्गौलाबाट बाहिरिन्छ। BUN ले urea मा रहेको nitrogen को मात्रा मापन गर्छ।","Clinical Biochemistry",{status:"reviewed",source:"MedlinePlus — BUN (Blood Urea Nitrogen)",url:"https://www.medlineplus.gov/lab-tests/bun-blood-urea-nitrogen/",basis:"Urea nitrogen is a waste product formed during protein breakdown"}],
  ["A dehydrated patient has an increased BUN. Which interpretation is most appropriate?","पानीको कमी भएको बिरामीमा BUN बढेको छ। सबैभन्दा उपयुक्त व्याख्या कुन हो?",["Dehydration can raise BUN; interpret with other renal tests and clinical findings","It proves chronic kidney failure","It confirms liver failure","It always indicates urinary infection"],0,"Dehydration can increase BUN, so an elevated result is not specific for kidney disease. Interpret it with creatinine, eGFR, hydration status and clinical findings.","Dehydration ले BUN बढाउन सक्छ, त्यसैले BUN बढ्दैमा kidney disease निश्चित हुँदैन। Creatinine, eGFR, hydration status र clinical अवस्थासँगै व्याख्या गर्नुपर्छ।","Clinical Biochemistry",{status:"reviewed",source:"MedlinePlus — BUN (Blood Urea Nitrogen)",url:"https://www.medlineplus.gov/lab-tests/bun-blood-urea-nitrogen/",basis:"Dehydration is one non-renal reason for increased BUN"}],
  ["Why is eGFR generally more informative about kidney filtration than serum creatinine alone?","Serum creatinine मात्रभन्दा eGFR ले kidney filtration बारे बढी जानकारी किन दिन्छ?",["It estimates filtration using creatinine and patient factors such as age and sex","It measures urine colour","It directly counts nephrons","It measures liver enzyme activity"],0,"Serum creatinine is used with factors such as age and sex in an equation to estimate glomerular filtration rate. Creatinine alone is influenced by muscle mass and other factors.","Serum creatinine लाई उमेर र sex जस्ता विवरणसँग equation मा प्रयोग गरेर eGFR अनुमान गरिन्छ। Creatinine मात्र muscle mass लगायतका कारणले प्रभावित हुन्छ।","Clinical Biochemistry",{status:"reviewed",source:"MedlinePlus — Creatinine Test",url:"https://medlineplus.gov/lab-tests/creatinine-test/",basis:"eGFR calculation uses creatinine and patient factors; more informative than creatinine alone"}],
  ["Which arterial blood gas pH value is within the usual reference interval?","कुन arterial blood gas pH सामान्य reference interval भित्र पर्छ?",["7.40","7.20","7.50","6.90"],0,"A commonly listed arterial blood pH reference interval is 7.35–7.45. Reference intervals can vary slightly by laboratory.","Arterial blood pH को सामान्य reference interval प्रायः 7.35–7.45 हुन्छ। Laboratory अनुसार reference interval केही फरक हुन सक्छ।","Clinical Biochemistry",{status:"reviewed",source:"MedlinePlus — Arterial Blood Gas (ABG) Test",url:"https://medlineplus.gov/lab-tests/arterial-blood-gas-abg-test/",basis:"ABG pH reference interval is listed as 7.35–7.45"}],
  ["An ABG report shows pH 7.28. This finding indicates:","ABG report मा pH 7.28 छ। यसले के जनाउँछ?",["Acidemia (blood pH below the usual range)","Alkalemia","Normal acid-base status","High oxygen saturation"],0,"A pH below 7.35 indicates acidemia. Identifying the primary respiratory or metabolic disorder requires considering PaCO2, bicarbonate and the clinical context.","pH 7.35 भन्दा कम हुँदा acidemia भनिन्छ। मुख्य समस्या respiratory हो वा metabolic भन्ने छुट्याउन PaCO2, bicarbonate र बिरामीको अवस्था हेर्नुपर्छ।","Clinical Biochemistry",{status:"reviewed",source:"MedlinePlus — Arterial Blood Gas (ABG) Test",url:"https://medlineplus.gov/lab-tests/arterial-blood-gas-abg-test/",basis:"ABG pH measures acidity; below the reference interval indicates acidemia"}],
  ["Which component of an ABG helps assess the metabolic contribution to acid-base balance?","Acid-base balance मा metabolic पक्ष मूल्याङ्कन गर्न ABG को कुन component उपयोगी हुन्छ?",["Bicarbonate (HCO3−)","PaO2 only","Oxygen saturation only","Haemoglobin colour"],0,"Bicarbonate is an electrolyte that helps regulate acid-base balance. ABG interpretation considers pH, PaCO2 and bicarbonate together rather than using one value alone.","Bicarbonate acid-base balance कायम राख्न सहयोग गर्ने electrolyte हो। ABG व्याख्या गर्दा pH, PaCO2 र bicarbonate तीनैलाई सँगै हेर्नुपर्छ।","Clinical Biochemistry",{status:"reviewed",source:"MedlinePlus — Arterial Blood Gas (ABG) Test",url:"https://medlineplus.gov/lab-tests/arterial-blood-gas-abg-test/",basis:"ABG may measure bicarbonate, which helps assess acid-base balance"}]
 ];

 // Clinical Biochemistry: electrolyte interpretation, checked against MedlinePlus and FDA reference material.
 const biochemistryReviewedBatch4=[
  ["A patient's total serum calcium is low and albumin is also markedly low. Which test best assesses the biologically active calcium fraction?","बिरामीको total serum calcium र albumin दुवै कम छन्। शरीरमा सक्रिय calcium fraction जाँच्न कुन परीक्षण उपयुक्त हुन्छ?",["Ionized calcium","Total cholesterol","Serum urea","Alkaline phosphatase"],0,"Ionized calcium measures the free, biologically active calcium that is not bound to proteins. Total calcium is affected by albumin concentration, so ionized calcium can clarify calcium status when protein levels are abnormal.","Ionized calcium ले protein सँग नबाँधिएको सक्रिय calcium मापन गर्छ। Albumin कम हुँदा total calcium पनि कम देखिन सक्छ, त्यसैले यस्तो अवस्थामा ionized calcium उपयोगी हुन्छ।","Clinical Biochemistry",{status:"reviewed",source:"MedlinePlus — Calcium Blood Test",url:"https://medlineplus.gov/lab-tests/calcium-blood-test/",basis:"Distinguishes protein-bound calcium from free, active ionized calcium"}],
  ["A patient reports tingling around the lips and muscle spasms. Which electrolyte abnormality should be considered?","बिरामीको ओठ वरिपरि झमझमाउने र मांसपेशी खुम्चिने समस्या छ। कुन electrolyte को कमी विचार गर्नुपर्छ?",["Hypocalcemia","Hypernatremia","Hyperphosphatemia","Hypermagnesemia"],0,"Low blood calcium can cause tingling around the lips and muscle cramps or spasms. Symptoms alone do not establish the diagnosis; laboratory testing and clinical assessment are needed.","रगतमा calcium कम हुँदा ओठ वरिपरि झमझमाउने, muscle cramp वा spasm हुन सक्छ। लक्षणले मात्र diagnosis निश्चित गर्दैन; lab test र clinical assessment आवश्यक हुन्छ।","Clinical Biochemistry",{status:"reviewed",source:"MedlinePlus — Calcium Blood Test",url:"https://medlineplus.gov/lab-tests/calcium-blood-test/",basis:"Lists tingling and muscle spasms among symptoms of low calcium"}],
  ["Which statement about serum phosphate is correct?","Serum phosphate सम्बन्धी कुन भनाइ सही हो?",["It supports bone and teeth structure and energy production","It is the main oxygen-carrying molecule","It is produced only by red blood cells","It has no role in nerve or muscle function"],0,"Phosphate is important for bones and teeth, energy production, nerve signalling and muscle contraction. Kidney function is an important factor in phosphate balance.","Phosphate हड्डी र दाँत, ऊर्जा उत्पादन, nerve signalling र muscle contraction का लागि महत्त्वपूर्ण हुन्छ। यसको सन्तुलनमा kidney को भूमिका महत्त्वपूर्ण हुन्छ।","Clinical Biochemistry",{status:"reviewed",source:"MedlinePlus — Phosphate in Blood",url:"https://medlineplus.gov/lab-tests/phosphate-in-blood/",basis:"Describes phosphate roles in bones, energy, nerves and muscles"}],
  ["A patient with an electrolyte panel has magnesium 1.2 mg/dL. Using the typical adult reference range of about 1.7–2.2 mg/dL, how should this result be described?","Electrolyte panel मा magnesium 1.2 mg/dL छ। वयस्कको सामान्य दायरा करिब 1.7–2.2 mg/dL मान्दा यो नतिजा के हो?",["Hypomagnesemia","Hypermagnesemia","Normal magnesium","Hypercalcemia"],0,"A magnesium level of 1.2 mg/dL is below the typical adult reference range and is described as hypomagnesemia. Reference intervals vary by laboratory, so use the reporting laboratory's range.","Magnesium 1.2 mg/dL सामान्य वयस्क दायराभन्दा कम भएकाले hypomagnesemia भनिन्छ। प्रयोगशालाअनुसार reference range फरक हुन सक्छ, त्यसैले रिपोर्टमा दिइएको दायरा हेर्नुपर्छ।","Clinical Biochemistry",{status:"reviewed",source:"MedlinePlus — Magnesium Blood Test",url:"https://medlineplus.gov/ency/article/003487.htm",basis:"Typical blood magnesium range is 1.7–2.2 mg/dL"}],
  ["A patient's serum sodium is 128 mEq/L. What is the correct laboratory term?","बिरामीको serum sodium 128 mEq/L छ। सही laboratory term कुन हो?",["Hyponatremia","Hypernatremia","Hyperkalemia","Hypercalcemia"],0,"A sodium concentration below the typical range of 135–145 mEq/L is called hyponatremia. Sodium results must be interpreted with fluid status, symptoms and the laboratory reference interval.","Sodium 135–145 mEq/L को सामान्य दायराभन्दा कम हुँदा hyponatremia भनिन्छ। यसको व्याख्या गर्दा शरीरको fluid status, लक्षण र lab reference range पनि हेर्नुपर्छ।","Clinical Biochemistry",{status:"reviewed",source:"MedlinePlus — Sodium Blood Test",url:"https://medlineplus.gov/ency/article/003481.htm",basis:"Gives a typical blood sodium range of 135–145 mEq/L"}],
  ["A patient has prolonged vomiting and an electrolyte panel is requested. Which statement is most accurate?","बिरामीलाई लामो समयदेखि बान्ता भइरहेको छ र electrolyte panel गरिएको छ। कुन भनाइ सबैभन्दा सही हो?",["Vomiting can contribute to electrolyte and fluid imbalance","Vomiting always causes hyperkalemia","Electrolyte testing is never useful after vomiting","Only calcium is affected by fluid loss"],0,"Vomiting and diarrhoea can contribute to fluid and electrolyte disturbances. An electrolyte panel helps assess relevant abnormalities, but results must be interpreted in the clinical context.","बान्ता र पखालाले शरीरको पानी तथा electrolyte सन्तुलन बिगार्न सक्छ। Electrolyte panel ले सम्भावित असन्तुलन जाँच्न मद्दत गर्छ, तर नतिजा बिरामीको अवस्थासँग मिलाएर व्याख्या गर्नुपर्छ।","Clinical Biochemistry",{status:"reviewed",source:"MedlinePlus — Electrolyte Panel",url:"https://medlineplus.gov/lab-tests/electrolyte-panel/",basis:"Notes vomiting and diarrhoea as causes of fluid/electrolyte changes"}]
 ];
 Q.push(...biochemistryReviewedBatch4); practiceQ.push(...biochemistryReviewedBatch4); mockQ.push(...biochemistryReviewedBatch4);

 // Clinical Haematology: CBC and red-cell indices questions checked against MedlinePlus and NCBI.
 const haematologyReviewedBatch1=[
  ["Which components are routinely included in a complete blood count (CBC)?","Complete Blood Count (CBC) मा सामान्यतया कुन-कुन कुरा समावेश हुन्छन्?",["RBC, WBC, platelets, haemoglobin and haematocrit","Only glucose and urea","Only electrolytes","Only liver enzymes"],0,"A CBC commonly measures red blood cells, white blood cells, platelets, haemoglobin and haematocrit. Many CBC reports also include red-cell indices such as MCV.","CBC मा सामान्यतया RBC, WBC, platelet, haemoglobin र haematocrit मापन गरिन्छ। धेरै CBC रिपोर्टमा MCV जस्ता red-cell indices पनि हुन्छन्।","Clinical Haematology",{status:"reviewed",source:"MedlinePlus — Complete Blood Count (CBC)",url:"https://www.medlineplus.gov/lab-tests/complete-blood-count-cbc/",basis:"Lists the principal CBC components and their roles"}],
  ["A CBC report shows MCV of 68 fL. Using a typical adult range of about 80–100 fL, how are the red cells classified by size?","CBC रिपोर्टमा MCV 68 fL छ। वयस्कको सामान्य दायरा करिब 80–100 fL मान्दा RBC को आकार कस्तो हुन्छ?",["Microcytic","Macrocytic","Normocytic","Spherocytic"],0,"An MCV below the laboratory reference interval indicates microcytosis, meaning the average red-cell volume is small. MCV alone does not establish the cause of anaemia.","MCV प्रयोगशालाको सामान्य दायराभन्दा कम हुँदा microcytosis अर्थात् RBC को औसत आकार सानो भएको जनाउँछ। MCV मात्रले anaemia को कारण निश्चित गर्दैन।","Clinical Haematology",{status:"reviewed",source:"MedlinePlus — Red Blood Cell (RBC) Indices",url:"https://medlineplus.gov/lab-tests/red-blood-cell-rbc-indices/",basis:"Defines MCV as average red-cell size and its role in anaemia classification"}],
  ["A patient's MCV is 108 fL. What is the size-based description of the red cells?","बिरामीको MCV 108 fL छ। RBC को आकारका आधारमा के भनिन्छ?",["Macrocytic","Microcytic","Normocytic","Hypochromic"],0,"An MCV above the laboratory reference interval indicates macrocytosis, meaning the average red-cell volume is increased. Further tests are needed to determine the cause.","MCV सामान्य दायराभन्दा बढी हुँदा macrocytosis अर्थात् RBC को औसत आकार ठूलो भएको जनाउँछ। कारण पत्ता लगाउन थप परीक्षण आवश्यक हुन्छ।","Clinical Haematology",{status:"reviewed",source:"MedlinePlus — Red Blood Cell (RBC) Indices",url:"https://medlineplus.gov/lab-tests/red-blood-cell-rbc-indices/",basis:"Explains MCV as a measure of average RBC size"}],
  ["Which red-cell index measures the average amount of haemoglobin in one red blood cell?","एउटा RBC मा रहेको haemoglobin को औसत मात्रा कुन red-cell index ले जनाउँछ?",["MCH","MCV","Hematocrit","RDW"],0,"Mean corpuscular haemoglobin (MCH) estimates the average amount of haemoglobin in an individual red blood cell. MCV measures cell volume, while MCHC measures haemoglobin concentration.","Mean corpuscular haemoglobin (MCH) ले एउटा RBC मा भएको haemoglobin को औसत मात्रा जनाउँछ। MCV ले cell volume र MCHC ले haemoglobin concentration जनाउँछ।","Clinical Haematology",{status:"reviewed",source:"MedlinePlus — CBC Blood Test",url:"https://medlineplus.gov/ency/article/003642.htm",basis:"Defines MCH, MCV and MCHC as distinct red-cell measurements"}],
  ["What is the primary role of platelets in haemostasis?","Haemostasis मा platelet को मुख्य भूमिका के हो?",["Forming a platelet plug at an injured blood vessel","Transporting oxygen","Producing antibodies","Carrying carbon dioxide only"],0,"Platelets help stop bleeding by adhering and aggregating at sites of vessel injury to form an initial platelet plug. Coagulation factors then help stabilise the clot.","रक्तनलीमा चोट लाग्दा platelet टाँसिने र एकआपसमा जम्मा भएर प्रारम्भिक platelet plug बनाउँछन्। त्यसपछि coagulation factors ले clot लाई स्थिर बनाउन सहयोग गर्छन्।","Clinical Haematology",{status:"reviewed",source:"MedlinePlus — Complete Blood Count (CBC)",url:"https://www.medlineplus.gov/lab-tests/complete-blood-count-cbc/",basis:"Describes platelets as blood components that help stop bleeding"}],
  ["A differential WBC count reports an increased proportion of neutrophils. Which term describes this finding?","Differential WBC count मा neutrophil को अनुपात बढेको छ। यस अवस्थालाई के भनिन्छ?",["Neutrophilia","Lymphopenia","Eosinopenia","Thrombocytopenia"],0,"An increased neutrophil count or proportion is called neutrophilia. It can occur in several settings, including some infections and inflammatory conditions, and is not by itself a definitive diagnosis.","Neutrophil को संख्या वा अनुपात बढ्नुलाई neutrophilia भनिन्छ। केही संक्रमण तथा inflammatory अवस्थाहरूमा यस्तो हुन सक्छ, तर यसले मात्र निश्चित diagnosis गर्दैन।","Clinical Haematology",{status:"reviewed",source:"NCBI Bookshelf — Normal and Abnormal CBC With Differential",url:"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK604207/",basis:"Discusses interpretation of differential white-cell counts"}],
  ["Which cells are counted as young, newly released red blood cells?","भर्खर bone marrow बाट रगतमा आएका अपरिपक्व RBC लाई के भनिन्छ?",["Reticulocytes","Neutrophils","Platelets","Monocytes"],0,"Reticulocytes are immature red blood cells recently released from the bone marrow. The reticulocyte count helps assess marrow response to anaemia or blood loss.","Reticulocyte भनेको bone marrow बाट भर्खर निस्केका अपरिपक्व RBC हुन्। Reticulocyte count ले anaemia वा blood loss प्रति bone marrow को प्रतिक्रिया बुझ्न मद्दत गर्छ।","Clinical Haematology",{status:"reviewed",source:"MedlinePlus — Blood Count Tests",url:"https://medlineplus.gov/bloodcounttests.html",basis:"Lists reticulocyte count among blood-count tests"}]
 ];
 Q.push(...haematologyReviewedBatch1); practiceQ.push(...haematologyReviewedBatch1); mockQ.push(...haematologyReviewedBatch1);

 // Clinical Haematology: anaemia patterns and peripheral smear interpretation.
 const haematologyReviewedBatch2=[
  ["A patient has microcytic hypochromic anaemia and a low serum ferritin. Which diagnosis is most strongly supported?","बिरामीमा microcytic hypochromic anaemia र serum ferritin कम छ। कुन diagnosis बढी सम्भावित हुन्छ?",["Iron deficiency anaemia","Vitamin B12 deficiency","Aplastic anaemia","Acute haemolysis"],0,"A low ferritin indicates reduced iron stores and strongly supports iron deficiency, although ferritin may be raised by inflammation. Interpret it with the clinical picture and other iron studies.","Ferritin कम हुनु शरीरमा iron store घटेको संकेत हो र iron deficiency लाई समर्थन गर्छ। तर inflammation हुँदा ferritin बढ्न सक्छ, त्यसैले अन्य iron studies र clinical अवस्था पनि हेर्नुपर्छ।","Clinical Haematology",{status:"reviewed",source:"MSD Manual — Iron Deficiency Anemia",url:"https://www.msdmanuals.com/professional/hematology/anemias-caused-by-deficient-erythropoiesis/iron-deficiency-anemia",basis:"Low ferritin supports depleted iron stores; interpret with iron studies"}],
  ["Which peripheral smear pattern is classically associated with iron deficiency anaemia?","Iron deficiency anaemia मा peripheral smear मा सामान्यतया कस्तो pattern देखिन्छ?",["Microcytic and hypochromic red cells","Macro-ovalocytes with hypersegmented neutrophils","Spherocytes only","Sickle-shaped red cells only"],0,"Iron deficiency commonly produces small (microcytic), pale (hypochromic) red cells. Anisopoikilocytosis and increased RDW may also be present.","Iron deficiency मा RBC साना (microcytic) र फिका (hypochromic) देखिन्छन्। Anisopoikilocytosis र RDW बढेको पनि हुन सक्छ।","Clinical Haematology",{status:"reviewed",source:"NCBI Bookshelf — Iron Deficiency and Microcytic Hypochromic Anemia",url:"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK560876/",basis:"Describes microcytosis, hypochromia and smear morphology in iron deficiency"}],
  ["In uncomplicated iron deficiency anaemia, which iron-study pattern is commonly expected?","जटिलता नभएको iron deficiency anaemia मा कुन iron-study pattern सामान्यतया अपेक्षित हुन्छ?",["Low ferritin and increased TIBC","High ferritin and low TIBC","High serum iron and high ferritin","Normal ferritin with increased serum iron"],0,"Iron deficiency typically causes low ferritin, low serum iron and increased total iron-binding capacity (TIBC). Transferrin saturation is usually reduced.","Iron deficiency मा सामान्यतया ferritin र serum iron कम तथा TIBC बढी हुन्छ। Transferrin saturation पनि प्रायः कम हुन्छ।","Clinical Haematology",{status:"reviewed",source:"MSD Manual — Iron Deficiency Anemia",url:"https://www.msdmanuals.com/professional/hematology/anemias-caused-by-deficient-erythropoiesis/iron-deficiency-anemia",basis:"Summarises typical iron, ferritin and iron-binding capacity pattern"}],
  ["A blood film shows macro-ovalocytes and hypersegmented neutrophils. Which type of anaemia should be suspected?","Blood film मा macro-ovalocytes र hypersegmented neutrophils देखिन्छन्। कुन प्रकारको anaemia शंका गर्नुपर्छ?",["Megaloblastic anaemia","Iron deficiency anaemia","Thalassaemia trait","Acute blood-loss anaemia"],0,"Macro-ovalocytes with hypersegmented neutrophils are characteristic clues to megaloblastic anaemia, commonly related to vitamin B12 or folate deficiency. Confirm with appropriate laboratory tests.","Macro-ovalocytes र hypersegmented neutrophils megaloblastic anaemia का महत्त्वपूर्ण संकेत हुन्। यो प्रायः vitamin B12 वा folate कमीका कारण हुन्छ; lab test बाट पुष्टि गर्नुपर्छ।","Clinical Haematology",{status:"reviewed",source:"NCBI Bookshelf — Anemia",url:"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK499994/",basis:"Describes macro-ovalocytes and hypersegmented neutrophils in megaloblastic anaemia"}],
  ["Which laboratory marker is expected to rise in vitamin B12 deficiency but usually remains normal in isolated folate deficiency?","Vitamin B12 deficiency मा बढ्ने तर folate deficiency मात्र हुँदा सामान्यतया नबढ्ने कुन marker हो?",["Methylmalonic acid (MMA)","Serum sodium","Serum albumin","Troponin"],0,"Methylmalonic acid is typically elevated in vitamin B12 deficiency, whereas it remains within the reference range in isolated folate deficiency. Homocysteine may rise in both conditions.","Vitamin B12 कमी हुँदा methylmalonic acid (MMA) सामान्यतया बढ्छ, तर folate कमी मात्र हुँदा सामान्य दायरामै रहन्छ। Homocysteine भने दुवै अवस्थामा बढ्न सक्छ।","Clinical Haematology",{status:"reviewed",source:"NCBI Bookshelf — Anemia",url:"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK499994/",basis:"Explains MMA and homocysteine patterns in B12 versus folate deficiency"}],
  ["A patient has marked microcytosis with a relatively high RBC count and target cells on the smear. Which condition should be considered?","बिरामीमा धेरै microcytosis, तुलनात्मक रूपमा RBC count बढी र smear मा target cells छन्। कुन अवस्था विचार गर्नुपर्छ?",["Thalassaemia","Iron deficiency alone","Vitamin B12 deficiency","Aplastic anaemia"],0,"Thalassaemia trait can show microcytosis with a normal or relatively high RBC count and target cells. Iron studies and haemoglobin analysis help distinguish it from iron deficiency; smear findings alone are not diagnostic.","Thalassaemia trait मा microcytosis सँगै RBC count सामान्य वा तुलनात्मक रूपमा बढी र target cells देखिन सक्छन्। Iron studies र haemoglobin analysis ले iron deficiency बाट छुट्याउन मद्दत गर्छ; smear मात्रले diagnosis पुष्टि गर्दैन।","Clinical Haematology",{status:"reviewed",source:"NCBI Bookshelf — Iron Deficiency and Microcytic Hypochromic Anemia",url:"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK560876/",basis:"Contrasts thalassaemia smear features and RBC count with iron deficiency"}],
  ["Which test is commonly used to evaluate suspected beta-thalassaemia trait?","Beta-thalassaemia trait शंका हुँदा कुन परीक्षण सामान्यतया प्रयोग गरिन्छ?",["Haemoglobin electrophoresis or haemoglobin analysis","Serum amylase","Bleeding time only","Urine ketone test"],0,"Haemoglobin analysis, including electrophoresis or HPLC, can identify an increased HbA2 pattern that supports beta-thalassaemia trait. The result should be interpreted with CBC and iron studies.","Haemoglobin electrophoresis वा HPLC जस्ता परीक्षणले HbA2 बढेको pattern देखाएर beta-thalassaemia trait पहिचान गर्न मद्दत गर्छन्। नतिजा CBC र iron studies सँग मिलाएर व्याख्या गर्नुपर्छ।","Clinical Haematology",{status:"reviewed",source:"NCBI — Approach to the diagnosis and classification of blood diseases",url:"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7152454/",basis:"Describes haemoglobin electrophoresis/HPLC and HbA2 in beta-thalassaemia diagnosis"}]
 ];
 Q.push(...haematologyReviewedBatch2); practiceQ.push(...haematologyReviewedBatch2); mockQ.push(...haematologyReviewedBatch2);

 // Clinical Haematology: WBC differential, ESR, reticulocytes and coagulation.
 const haematologyReviewedBatch3=[
  ["Which WBC type is commonly increased in many acute bacterial infections?","धेरै acute bacterial infection मा कुन WBC सामान्यतया बढ्न सक्छ?",["Neutrophils","Eosinophils","Basophils","Lymphocytes only"],0,"Neutrophilia is commonly seen in many acute bacterial infections, but it is not specific and must be interpreted with symptoms and other findings.","धेरै acute bacterial infection मा neutrophil बढ्न सक्छ। तर यो कुनै एक रोगका लागि मात्र विशिष्ट होइन; लक्षण र अन्य जाँचसँगै व्याख्या गर्नुपर्छ।","Clinical Haematology",{status:"reviewed",source:"NCBI Bookshelf — Leukocyte Disorders",url:"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK560882/",basis:"Reviews neutrophil responses and leukocyte abnormalities"}],
  ["Which WBC is most associated with allergic responses and many parasitic infections?","एलर्जी प्रतिक्रिया र धेरै परजीवी संक्रमणसँग कुन WBC बढी सम्बन्धित हुन्छ?",["Eosinophils","Neutrophils","Monocytes","Platelets"],0,"Eosinophils can increase in allergic disorders and some parasitic infections, especially tissue-invasive helminths. Eosinophilia has other causes too.","एलर्जी र केही परजीवी संक्रमण, विशेषगरी tissue-invasive helminths मा eosinophil बढ्न सक्छ। Eosinophilia का अन्य कारण पनि हुन्छन्।","Clinical Haematology",{status:"reviewed",source:"Merck Manual — Eosinophilic Disorders",url:"https://www.merckmanuals.com/professional/hematology-and-oncology/eosinophilic-disorders/eosinophilia",basis:"Describes allergic and parasitic causes of eosinophilia"}],
  ["Which test is commonly used as a nonspecific marker of inflammation?","Inflammation को nonspecific marker का रूपमा कुन परीक्षण प्रयोग हुन्छ?",["ESR","ABO grouping","Bleeding time","Reticulocyte count"],0,"The erythrocyte sedimentation rate (ESR) is a nonspecific marker that may rise with inflammation. It cannot identify the cause or diagnose a specific disease on its own.","ESR inflammation हुँदा बढ्न सक्ने nonspecific marker हो। यसले एक्लै रोगको कारण वा निश्चित diagnosis बताउँदैन।","Clinical Haematology",{status:"reviewed",source:"MedlinePlus — ESR Test",url:"https://medlineplus.gov/lab-tests/erythrocyte-sedimentation-rate-esr/",basis:"Explains ESR as a nonspecific indicator of inflammation"}],
  ["A patient with anaemia has a markedly increased reticulocyte count. What does this most commonly suggest about marrow response?","Anaemia भएको बिरामीमा reticulocyte count धेरै बढेको छ। यसले bone marrow को कस्तो प्रतिक्रिया जनाउँछ?",["An increased red-cell production response","Complete absence of marrow activity","Reduced platelet production only","A diagnosis of iron deficiency by itself"],0,"A raised reticulocyte count indicates increased release of young red cells and often reflects marrow response to blood loss or haemolysis. It must be interpreted with the clinical context.","Reticulocyte count बढ्नु भनेको नयाँ RBC उत्पादन/रिलिज बढेको संकेत हो; blood loss वा haemolysis पछि यस्तो हुन सक्छ। Clinical अवस्थासँग मिलाएर बुझ्नुपर्छ।","Clinical Haematology",{status:"reviewed",source:"MedlinePlus — Reticulocyte Count",url:"https://medlineplus.gov/lab-tests/reticulocyte-count/",basis:"Describes reticulocytes as young RBCs and their use in evaluating marrow response"}],
  ["Which coagulation test is commonly used to monitor unfractionated heparin therapy?","Unfractionated heparin उपचारको निगरानी गर्न सामान्यतया कुन coagulation test प्रयोग हुन्छ?",["aPTT","PT only","ESR","Bleeding time"],0,"Activated partial thromboplastin time (aPTT) is commonly used to monitor unfractionated heparin, although anti-Xa testing is used in some settings and local protocols vary.","Unfractionated heparin को निगरानीका लागि aPTT सामान्यतया प्रयोग हुन्छ। केही अवस्थामा anti-Xa परीक्षण पनि प्रयोग गरिन्छ र स्थानीय protocol फरक हुन सक्छ।","Clinical Haematology",{status:"reviewed",source:"MedlinePlus — PTT Test",url:"https://medlineplus.gov/lab-tests/partial-thromboplastin-time-ptt-test/",basis:"Explains PTT/aPTT use in assessing clotting and heparin monitoring"}],
  ["Which test is routinely used to monitor warfarin anticoagulant therapy?","Warfarin anticoagulant उपचारको निगरानी गर्न कुन परीक्षण प्रयोग गरिन्छ?",["PT/INR","aPTT only","ESR","Platelet count only"],0,"Prothrombin time reported as the international normalized ratio (PT/INR) is used to monitor warfarin therapy. The target INR depends on the indication and clinician's plan.","Warfarin उपचारको निगरानीका लागि PT लाई INR का रूपमा रिपोर्ट गरिन्छ। लक्ष्य INR बिरामीको रोग र चिकित्सकीय योजनाअनुसार फरक हुन्छ।","Clinical Haematology",{status:"reviewed",source:"MedlinePlus — Prothrombin Time Test and INR",url:"https://medlineplus.gov/lab-tests/prothrombin-time-test-and-inr-ptinr/",basis:"Describes PT/INR monitoring for warfarin"}],
  ["A patient has prolonged PT and normal aPTT. Which pathway is primarily assessed by PT?","बिरामीको PT लामो र aPTT सामान्य छ। PT ले मुख्य रूपमा कुन pathway जाँच्छ?",["Extrinsic and common pathways","Intrinsic pathway only","Fibrinolytic pathway only","Platelet adhesion only"],0,"PT evaluates the extrinsic and common coagulation pathways, while aPTT evaluates the intrinsic and common pathways. Results should be interpreted with the clinical history and laboratory method.","PT ले extrinsic र common coagulation pathway जाँच्छ भने aPTT ले intrinsic र common pathway जाँच्छ। नतिजा clinical history र laboratory method अनुसार व्याख्या गर्नुपर्छ।","Clinical Haematology",{status:"reviewed",source:"MedlinePlus — Prothrombin Time Test and INR",url:"https://medlineplus.gov/lab-tests/prothrombin-time-test-and-inr-ptinr/",basis:"Describes PT assessment of blood clotting"}]
 ];
