 // Clinical Microbiology & Immunology: core staining, culture media and biosafety.
 const microbiologyReviewedBatch1=[
  ["What is the correct sequence of reagents in a standard Gram stain?","Standard Gram stain मा reagent प्रयोग गर्ने सही क्रम कुन हो?",["Crystal violet → iodine → decolorizer → safranin","Safranin → iodine → crystal violet → decolorizer","Iodine → safranin → decolorizer → crystal violet","Decolorizer → crystal violet → safranin → iodine"],0,"The standard sequence is crystal violet (primary stain), Gram's iodine (mordant), alcohol/acetone decolorizer, and safranin (counterstain).","सही क्रम: Crystal violet (primary stain), Gram's iodine (mordant), alcohol/acetone (decolorizer), अनि safranin (counterstain) हो।","Clinical Microbiology",{status:"reviewed",source:"American Society for Microbiology — Gram Stain Protocols",url:"https://asm.org/protocols/gram-stain-protocols",basis:"Lists the four basic Gram-stain steps"}],
  ["After a correctly performed Gram stain, Gram-positive bacteria usually appear which colour?","सही Gram stain पछि Gram-positive bacteria सामान्यतया कुन रङका देखिन्छन्?",["Purple/violet","Pink/red","Green","Colourless"],0,"Gram-positive bacteria retain the crystal violet–iodine complex during decolorization and appear purple or violet.","Gram-positive bacteria ले decolorization पछि पनि crystal violet–iodine complex राख्छन्, त्यसैले बैजनी/purple देखिन्छन्।","Clinical Microbiology",{status:"reviewed",source:"NCBI Bookshelf — Gram Staining",url:"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK10755/",basis:"Explains retention of crystal violet by Gram-positive cell walls"}],
  ["A Gram-negative organism usually appears which colour after counterstaining?","Counterstain गरेपछि Gram-negative organism सामान्यतया कुन रङको देखिन्छ?",["Pink/red","Purple","Blue-black","Yellow"],0,"Gram-negative bacteria are decolorized by alcohol/acetone and then take up the safranin counterstain, appearing pink to red.","Gram-negative bacteria alcohol/acetone ले decolorize भएपछि safranin counterstain लिन्छन् र pink/red देखिन्छन्।","Clinical Microbiology",{status:"reviewed",source:"American Society for Microbiology — Gram Stain Protocols",url:"https://asm.org/protocols/gram-stain-protocols",basis:"Describes Gram-negative organisms as pink after counterstaining"}],
  ["A stool culture isolate produces pink colonies on MacConkey agar. What does this most directly indicate?","Stool culture को isolate MacConkey agar मा pink colony बनाउँछ। यसले मुख्यतः के जनाउँछ?",["Lactose fermentation by a Gram-negative organism","Growth of a Gram-positive organism","Spore formation","Acid-fastness"],0,"MacConkey agar selects mainly for Gram-negative bacteria and differentiates lactose fermenters; acid production turns the neutral-red indicator pink. Colony colour is presumptive, not final species identification.","MacConkey agar ले मुख्यतः Gram-negative bacteria छान्छ र lactose fermentation छुट्याउँछ। Acid बनेपछि neutral-red indicator pink हुन्छ। Colony को रङ presumptive हो, अन्तिम species identification होइन।","Clinical Microbiology",{status:"reviewed",source:"NCBI Bookshelf — MacConkey Medium",url:"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK557394/",basis:"Explains selective action and pink lactose-fermenting colonies"}],
  ["Which method uses saturated steam under pressure to sterilize suitable laboratory materials?","उपयुक्त laboratory सामग्री sterilize गर्न pressure सहित saturated steam प्रयोग गर्ने विधि कुन हो?",["Autoclaving","Hot-air oven only","Filtration only","Sun drying"],0,"An autoclave uses saturated steam under pressure. A commonly used cycle for suitable clean items is around 121°C for 15 minutes, but the validated cycle depends on the load, packaging and equipment instructions.","Autoclave ले pressure सहित saturated steam प्रयोग गर्छ। उपयुक्त clean सामग्रीका लागि 121°C मा करिब 15 मिनेट सामान्य cycle हो; तर load, packaging र उपकरणको निर्देशनअनुसार validated cycle फरक हुन सक्छ।","Clinical Microbiology",{status:"reviewed",source:"WHO — Toolkit SOP: Performance, Quality and Monitoring of Autoclave",url:"https://cdn.who.int/media/docs/default-source/antimicrobial-resistance/hq-amr/toolkit-of-standard-operating-procedures-for-bacteriology--mycology-and-antimicrobial-susceptibility-testing/final-sops/q04---performance-quality-and-monitoring-of-autoclave.pdf",basis:"Gives typical 121°C sterilization cycle and stresses cycle validation"}],
  ["Which practice is essential to reduce contamination while transferring a bacterial culture?","Bacterial culture transfer गर्दा contamination घटाउन कुन अभ्यास आवश्यक हुन्छ?",["Aseptic technique with sterile tools and media","Reusing an unsterilized loop","Leaving culture plates open","Mouth pipetting"],0,"Aseptic technique uses sterile tools and media and minimizes unnecessary exposure of cultures to the environment. It helps prevent contamination and cross-contamination.","Aseptic technique मा sterile उपकरण र media प्रयोग गरिन्छ र culture लाई वातावरणमा अनावश्यक खुला राखिँदैन। यसले contamination तथा cross-contamination रोक्न मद्दत गर्छ।","Clinical Microbiology",{status:"reviewed",source:"ATCC — Introduction to Microbiology",url:"https://www.atcc.org/resources/culture-guides/introduction-to-microbiology",basis:"Recommends sterile tools/media and minimizing exposure during culture handling"}],
  ["How should contaminated needles and other laboratory sharps be discarded?","Contaminated needle तथा अन्य laboratory sharps कसरी फाल्नुपर्छ?",["In a puncture-resistant sharps container","In an open general-waste bin","In a paper bag","By recapping and placing on the bench"],0,"Contaminated sharps should be segregated and placed in a puncture-proof, closable container; they must not be discarded loose in general waste. Follow local biomedical-waste rules.","Contaminated sharps लाई छुट्टै puncture-proof र बन्द गर्न मिल्ने container मा राख्नुपर्छ। General waste मा खुला फाल्नु हुँदैन; स्थानीय biomedical-waste नियम पालना गर्नुपर्छ।","Clinical Microbiology",{status:"reviewed",source:"WHO — Laboratory Biosafety Manual, Decontamination and Waste Management",url:"https://www.who.int/publications/i/item/9789240011359",basis:"Covers segregation and safe management of contaminated sharps and laboratory waste"}]
 ];
 Q.push(...microbiologyReviewedBatch1); practiceQ.push(...microbiologyReviewedBatch1); mockQ.push(...microbiologyReviewedBatch1);

 // Clinical Microbiology: culture media, morphology and antimicrobial susceptibility.
 const microbiologyReviewedBatch2=[
  ["Which culture medium is commonly used to observe alpha, beta and gamma haemolysis?","Alpha, beta र gamma haemolysis हेर्न सामान्यतया कुन culture medium प्रयोग गरिन्छ?",["Blood agar","MacConkey agar","Nutrient broth only","Sabouraud agar"],0,"Blood agar is an enriched medium and can differentiate organisms by haemolysis around colonies: alpha (partial), beta (complete) and gamma (no haemolysis).","Blood agar enriched medium हो र colony वरिपरिको haemolysis अनुसार छुट्याउन सकिन्छ: alpha (आंशिक), beta (पूर्ण) र gamma (haemolysis नहुने)।","Clinical Microbiology",{status:"reviewed",source:"CDC OneLab REACH — Basic Culture Media and Isolation Techniques",url:"https://reach.cdc.gov/sites/default/files/job-aids-resources/culture-media-table-508.pdf",basis:"Classifies blood agar as enriched and differential medium"}],
  ["Why is chocolate agar useful for fastidious bacteria such as Haemophilus species?","Haemophilus जस्ता fastidious bacteria का लागि chocolate agar किन उपयोगी हुन्छ?",["Heated blood releases growth factors needed by some organisms","It contains a high concentration of salt","It prevents all bacterial growth","It is used only for fungi"],0,"Chocolate agar is an enriched medium made with heated blood; red-cell lysis releases nutrients such as X and V factors that support certain fastidious organisms. It is not named for containing chocolate.","Chocolate agar heated blood बाट बनाइएको enriched medium हो। RBC फुट्दा X र V जस्ता growth factors उपलब्ध हुन्छन्, जसले केही fastidious organism बढ्न सहयोग गर्छ। यसमा खाने chocolate हुँदैन।","Clinical Microbiology",{status:"reviewed",source:"CDC — Selected Examples of Media for Primary Isolation",url:"https://stacks.cdc.gov/view/cdc/7700/cdc_7700_DS1.pdf",basis:"Describes chocolate agar as enriched medium for Haemophilus and Neisseria"}],
  ["Mannitol salt agar is selective mainly because it contains which component?","Mannitol salt agar मुख्यतः कुन पदार्थका कारण selective हुन्छ?",["High concentration of sodium chloride","Bile salts only","Blood cells","Urea"],0,"The high salt concentration of mannitol salt agar inhibits many bacteria while allowing salt-tolerant organisms, especially staphylococci, to grow. Mannitol fermentation can then be differentiated by the indicator.","Mannitol salt agar मा sodium chloride को मात्रा धेरै हुन्छ, जसले धेरै bacteria रोक्छ तर salt-tolerant Staphylococci बढ्न सक्छन्। Mannitol fermentation indicator बाट छुट्याउन सकिन्छ।","Clinical Microbiology",{status:"reviewed",source:"Michigan State University — Cultivation Media for Bacteria",url:"https://learn.chm.msu.edu/vibl/content/differential/index.html",basis:"Explains high-salt selectivity of mannitol salt agar"}],
  ["Which bacterial shape is described as spherical or round?","गोलो वा spherical आकार भएको bacteria लाई के भनिन्छ?",["Coccus","Bacillus","Spirillum","Vibrio"],0,"Cocci are spherical or round bacterial cells. Bacilli are rod-shaped, while spiral forms include spirilla and spirochetes; vibrio are comma-shaped.","Cocci गोलो आकारका bacteria हुन्। Bacilli rod-shaped हुन्छन्; spirilla/spirochetes spiral र vibrio comma-shaped हुन्छन्।","Clinical Microbiology",{status:"reviewed",source:"ATCC — Introduction to Microbiology: Morphology",url:"https://www.atcc.org/resources/culture-guides/introduction-to-microbiology",basis:"Defines common bacterial cell shapes including cocci and bacilli"}],
  ["In the Kirby–Bauer disk diffusion test, what is measured around an antibiotic disk?","Kirby–Bauer disk diffusion test मा antibiotic disk वरिपरि के नापिन्छ?",["Diameter of the zone of inhibition","Colour of the agar only","Weight of the bacterial colony","Number of red blood cells"],0,"The diameter of the inhibition zone is measured in millimetres and interpreted using the applicable standardized breakpoint tables for that organism and antibiotic. Zone size alone should not be judged without the standard.","Inhibition zone को diameter millimetre मा नापिन्छ र सम्बन्धित organism तथा antibiotic का standardized breakpoint table अनुसार व्याख्या गरिन्छ। Standard बिना zone ठूलो/सानो मात्र हेरेर निष्कर्ष निकाल्नु हुँदैन।","Clinical Microbiology",{status:"reviewed",source:"EUCAST — Disk Diffusion and Quality Control",url:"https://www.eucast.org/bacteria/methodology-and-instructions/disk-diffusion-and-quality-control/",basis:"Describes standardized disk diffusion and breakpoint interpretation"}],
  ["What does the minimum inhibitory concentration (MIC) represent?","Minimum inhibitory concentration (MIC) ले के जनाउँछ?",["Lowest antimicrobial concentration that prevents visible growth under defined test conditions","Highest antibiotic dose tolerated by a patient","Number of bacteria in one colony","Time required for Gram staining"],0,"MIC is the lowest concentration of an antimicrobial that inhibits visible growth of the organism under defined in-vitro test conditions. It is interpreted with organism-specific breakpoints.","MIC भनेको निश्चित in-vitro परीक्षण अवस्थामा organism को देखिने growth रोक्ने सबैभन्दा कम antimicrobial concentration हो। यसलाई organism-specific breakpoint अनुसार व्याख्या गरिन्छ।","Clinical Microbiology",{status:"reviewed",source:"EUCAST — Disk Diffusion and Quality Control",url:"https://www.eucast.org/bacteria/methodology-and-instructions/disk-diffusion-and-quality-control/",basis:"Identifies MIC as the basis of antimicrobial susceptibility testing"}],
  ["Why must a pure bacterial culture be used for a standardized disk diffusion susceptibility test?","Standard disk diffusion susceptibility test मा pure bacterial culture किन चाहिन्छ?",["To ensure the measured response belongs to one organism","To increase contamination","To avoid measuring inhibition zones","To replace quality control"],0,"A standardized disk diffusion test uses a pure, correctly identified isolate and a standardized inoculum. Mixed cultures can produce misleading inhibition zones and invalid interpretation.","Standard disk diffusion test का लागि pure र सही पहिचान गरिएको isolate तथा standardized inoculum चाहिन्छ। Mixed culture भए inhibition zone गलत हुन सक्छ र interpretation अमान्य हुन सक्छ।","Clinical Microbiology",{status:"reviewed",source:"EUCAST — Disk Diffusion and Quality Control",url:"https://www.eucast.org/bacteria/methodology-and-instructions/disk-diffusion-and-quality-control/",basis:"Requires standardized methods and quality control for reliable susceptibility results"}]
 ];
