 // Clinical Microbiology & Immunology: specimen collection, transport and immune basics.
 const microbiologyReviewedBatch3=[
  ["For routine urine culture, which collection method best reduces contamination in a cooperative adult?","सामान्य urine culture का लागि सहयोग गर्न सक्ने वयस्कमा contamination कम गर्ने राम्रो collection विधि कुन हो?",["Clean-catch midstream urine","First drops of urine in an unclean container","Urine collected from the floor","Urine mixed with water"],0,"A clean-catch midstream specimen reduces contamination from skin and distal urethral flora. Use a sterile, properly labelled container and follow local collection instructions.","Clean-catch midstream urine ले छाला र बाहिरी urethra का जीवाणुबाट हुने contamination कम गर्छ। Sterile र सही label भएको container प्रयोग गरी स्थानीय निर्देशन पालना गर्नुपर्छ।","Clinical Microbiology",{status:"reviewed",source:"IDSA/ASM — Guide to Utilization of the Microbiology Laboratory (2024)",url:"https://academic.oup.com/cid/advance-article/doi/10.1093/cid/ciae104/7619499",basis:"Provides specimen-specific collection and transport recommendations"}],
  ["Which sputum specimen is most appropriate for routine bacterial culture in a patient with a productive cough?","खकार आउने बिरामीमा routine bacterial culture का लागि कुन sputum नमुना उपयुक्त हुन्छ?",["Deep-cough sputum from the lower respiratory tract","Saliva collected from the mouth","A nasal swab placed in a urine cup","Any fluid from the drinking glass"],0,"A good sputum specimen is produced by a deep cough from the lower respiratory tract, not saliva. Specimen quality and prompt transport affect culture interpretation.","राम्रो sputum नमुना गहिरो खोकीबाट lower respiratory tract बाट निस्किएको हुनुपर्छ, मुखको र्‍याल होइन। नमुनाको गुणस्तर र छिटो transport ले culture नतिजामा असर गर्छ।","Clinical Microbiology",{status:"reviewed",source:"IDSA/ASM — Guide to Utilization of the Microbiology Laboratory (2024)",url:"https://academic.oup.com/cid/advance-article/doi/10.1093/cid/ciae104/7619499",basis:"Specimen guidance emphasizes appropriate respiratory specimen type and handling"}],
  ["When should a microbiology specimen be labelled with patient identifiers?","Microbiology specimen मा बिरामीको पहिचान विवरण कहिले राख्नुपर्छ?",["At the time of collection, at the patient's side","Only after the result is available","Only when it reaches the referral laboratory","Never; the request form is enough"],0,"Label the specimen at collection using the required patient identifiers and match it with the request form. Unlabelled or mismatched specimens can lead to patient-safety errors.","नमुना संकलन गर्ने समयमा बिरामीकै छेउमा आवश्यक पहिचान विवरण राख्नुपर्छ र request form सँग मिलाउनुपर्छ। Label नभएको वा विवरण नमिलेको नमुनाले बिरामी सुरक्षामा जोखिम ल्याउँछ।","Clinical Microbiology",{status:"reviewed",source:"WHO — Laboratory Quality Management System Handbook",url:"https://www.who.int/publications-detail-redirect/9789241548274",basis:"Specimen management and identification are core pre-examination quality requirements"}],
  ["What is the key principle when choosing transport temperature and time for a microbiology specimen?","Microbiology specimen को transport temperature र समय छान्दा मुख्य सिद्धान्त के हो?",["Follow organism- and specimen-specific laboratory guidance","Keep every specimen frozen","Keep every specimen in direct sunlight","Use the same temperature for all specimens"],0,"Transport requirements vary by specimen and suspected organism. Incorrect temperature or delay can reduce pathogen recovery; consult the receiving laboratory's validated instructions.","Transport को आवश्यकता specimen र शंका गरिएको organism अनुसार फरक हुन्छ। गलत तापक्रम वा ढिलाइले pathogen पत्ता लाग्ने सम्भावना घटाउन सक्छ; receiving laboratory को validated निर्देशन पालना गर्नुपर्छ।","Clinical Microbiology",{status:"reviewed",source:"WHO — Laboratory Biosafety Manual, 4th edition",url:"https://iris.who.int/bitstream/handle/10665/337959/9789240011373-eng.pdf",basis:"Specimen transport conditions and duration can affect specimen quality and diagnostic sensitivity"}],
  ["What are the three layers of the standard triple packaging system for infectious substances?","Infectious substances को standard triple packaging system का तीन तह कुन हुन्?",["Leak-proof primary receptacle, leak-proof secondary packaging, rigid outer packaging","One paper envelope, one open tray, one cloth bag","Three unsealed plastic bags","Only a rigid outer box"],0,"Triple packaging uses a leak-proof primary receptacle, a leak-proof secondary package with absorbent material for liquids, and a strong rigid outer package. Follow current transport regulations and training.","Triple packaging मा leak-proof primary receptacle, तरल पदार्थ चुहिए सोस्ने सामग्रीसहित leak-proof secondary package, र बलियो rigid outer package हुन्छ। हाल लागू transport नियम र तालिम पालना गर्नुपर्छ।","Clinical Microbiology",{status:"reviewed",source:"WHO — Guidance on Regulations for the Transport of Infectious Substances 2025–2026",url:"https://www.who.int/publications/i/item/9789240120822",basis:"Current WHO guidance describes triple packaging, labelling and documentation"}],
  ["Which statement best describes innate immunity?","Innate immunity लाई सबैभन्दा राम्रोसँग कुन भनाइले वर्णन गर्छ?",["Immediate, broad defence without antigen-specific memory","A response that develops only after vaccination","Antibody production by plasma cells only","A response that always takes weeks to begin"],0,"Innate immunity provides rapid, broad initial defence through barriers, phagocytes, natural killer cells and soluble mediators. It does not create the same antigen-specific memory as adaptive immunity.","Innate immunity ले छिटो र व्यापक प्रारम्भिक सुरक्षा दिन्छ; यसमा barriers, phagocytes, natural killer cells र soluble mediators पर्छन्। यसले adaptive immunity जस्तो antigen-specific memory बनाउँदैन।","Immunology",{status:"reviewed",source:"NCBI Bookshelf — Physiology, Immune Response (updated 2025)",url:"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/sites/books/NBK539801/",basis:"Distinguishes rapid nonspecific innate defence from adaptive immune memory"}],
  ["Which cells differentiate into plasma cells and produce antibodies?","कुन कोशिका plasma cell मा परिवर्तन भएर antibody उत्पादन गर्छन्?",["B lymphocytes","Neutrophils","Platelets","Red blood cells"],0,"Activated B lymphocytes can differentiate into plasma cells, which secrete antibodies. Antibodies bind specific antigens and support immune defence.","Activated B lymphocytes plasma cells मा परिवर्तन हुन सक्छन् र plasma cells ले antibodies उत्पादन गर्छन्। Antibody ले specific antigen सँग bind गरी प्रतिरक्षामा सहयोग गर्छ।","Immunology",{status:"reviewed",source:"NCBI Bookshelf — Immunology Overview",url:"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/sites/books/NBK7795/",basis:"Describes B lymphocytes and antibody-producing plasma cells"}]
 ];
 Q.push(...microbiologyReviewedBatch3); practiceQ.push(...microbiologyReviewedBatch3); mockQ.push(...microbiologyReviewedBatch3);

 // Clinical Microbiology: important pathogens and immunological laboratory tests.
 const microbiologyReviewedBatch4=[
  ["Which staining property is characteristic of Mycobacterium tuberculosis?","Mycobacterium tuberculosis को विशेष staining गुण कुन हो?",["Acid-fastness","Gram-negative diplococci","Spore-forming rods","Non-staining cocci"],0,"Mycobacteria have a lipid-rich cell wall containing mycolic acids and retain primary stain after acid-alcohol decolorization; they are described as acid-fast bacilli (AFB).","Mycobacteria को cell wall मा mycolic acid हुन्छ र acid-alcohol ले decolorize गर्दा पनि stain कायम राख्छन्। त्यसैले acid-fast bacilli (AFB) भनिन्छ।","Clinical Microbiology",{status:"reviewed",source:"CDC — Clinical and Laboratory Diagnosis for Tuberculosis",url:"https://www.cdc.gov/tb/hcp/testing-diagnosis/clinical-and-laboratory-diagnosis.html",basis:"Describes AFB smear microscopy and acid-fast organisms"}],
  ["A sputum smear is AFB-positive. Which statement is correct?","Sputum smear AFB-positive आयो। कुन भनाइ सही हो?",["It suggests mycobacteria but does not by itself confirm M. tuberculosis","It proves drug-sensitive tuberculosis","It excludes nontuberculous mycobacteria","It makes culture unnecessary"],0,"An AFB-positive smear can indicate mycobacteria, but it does not identify M. tuberculosis specifically; nontuberculous mycobacteria may also be acid-fast. Culture and/or molecular tests are needed for further identification.","AFB-positive smear ले mycobacteria भएको संकेत गर्छ, तर M. tuberculosis नै हो भनेर एक्लै पुष्टि गर्दैन; अन्य mycobacteria पनि acid-fast हुन सक्छन्। थप पहिचानका लागि culture वा molecular test आवश्यक हुन्छ।","Clinical Microbiology",{status:"reviewed",source:"CDC — Examination of Smears for AFB",url:"https://www.cdc.gov/tb/webcourses/TB101/page17012.html",basis:"States positive AFB smear does not confirm TB and culture is needed"}],
  ["What does the Xpert MTB/RIF assay detect from a suitable specimen?","उपयुक्त नमुनाबाट Xpert MTB/RIF assay ले के पत्ता लगाउँछ?",["M. tuberculosis complex and genetic markers associated with rifampicin resistance","Only bacterial colony colour","Only patient antibodies to TB","All antibiotic resistance genes"],0,"Xpert MTB/RIF is a nucleic acid amplification test that detects M. tuberculosis complex and mutations associated with rifampicin resistance. It does not replace all culture and drug-susceptibility testing.","Xpert MTB/RIF nucleic acid amplification test हो। यसले M. tuberculosis complex र rifampicin resistance सँग सम्बन्धित genetic mutation पत्ता लगाउँछ। यसले सबै culture तथा drug-susceptibility परीक्षणलाई प्रतिस्थापन गर्दैन।","Clinical Microbiology",{status:"reviewed",source:"CDC — Xpert MTB/RIF Assay",url:"https://www.cdc.gov/tb/php/laboratory-information/xpert-mtb-rif-assay.html",basis:"Describes simultaneous MTBC detection and rifampin-resistance detection"}],
  ["Which specimen is commonly cultured to confirm intestinal Salmonella infection?","आन्द्रासम्बन्धी Salmonella infection पुष्टि गर्न सामान्यतया कुन नमुना culture गरिन्छ?",["Stool","Hair","Nail clipping","Sputum"],0,"Stool culture is commonly used to diagnose Salmonella gastroenteritis. Culture provides an isolate for further identification and antimicrobial susceptibility testing when indicated.","Salmonella gastroenteritis पत्ता लगाउन stool culture सामान्यतया प्रयोग हुन्छ। Culture बाट isolate प्राप्त हुन्छ, जसलाई थप पहिचान र आवश्यक परे antimicrobial susceptibility testing गर्न सकिन्छ।","Clinical Microbiology",{status:"reviewed",source:"CDC — Clinical Overview of Salmonellosis",url:"https://www.cdc.gov/salmonella/hcp/clinical-overview/index.html",basis:"Recommends culture for diagnosis and obtaining isolates"}],
  ["Gram-positive cocci in clusters that are catalase-positive and coagulase-positive are most consistent with which organism?","Gram-positive cocci clusters मा देखिन्छ, catalase-positive र coagulase-positive छ। कुन organism सँग बढी मिल्छ?",["Staphylococcus aureus","Streptococcus pyogenes","Enterococcus faecalis","Neisseria gonorrhoeae"],0,"Staphylococci are catalase-positive cocci that commonly form clusters. Coagulase positivity supports identification of S. aureus; confirmatory identification should follow the laboratory's validated algorithm.","Staphylococci catalase-positive cocci हुन् र प्रायः cluster मा देखिन्छन्। Coagulase-positive नतिजाले S. aureus पहिचानलाई समर्थन गर्छ; अन्तिम पुष्टि laboratory को validated algorithm अनुसार गर्नुपर्छ।","Clinical Microbiology",{status:"reviewed",source:"CDC — Staphylococci Identification Chart",url:"https://reach.cdc.gov/sites/default/files/job-aids-resources/Staphylococci_ID_Chart_Branded_508.pdf",basis:"Shows Gram-positive cocci clusters, catalase-positive and coagulase testing for S. aureus"}],
  ["Which laboratory finding is typical of Streptococcus pyogenes on blood agar?","Blood agar मा Streptococcus pyogenes को सामान्य विशेषता कुन हो?",["Beta-haemolytic colonies and Gram-positive cocci in chains","Green colonies and Gram-negative rods","Non-haemolytic Gram-negative diplococci","Acid-fast branching rods"],0,"S. pyogenes typically appears as Gram-positive cocci in chains and produces beta-haemolytic colonies on blood agar. PYR and Lancefield group A antigen testing can support identification.","S. pyogenes सामान्यतया chain मा रहेका Gram-positive cocci हुन् र blood agar मा beta-haemolysis देखाउँछन्। PYR तथा Lancefield group A antigen test ले पहिचानमा सहयोग गर्छ।","Clinical Microbiology",{status:"reviewed",source:"NCBI Bookshelf — Laboratory Diagnosis of Streptococcus pyogenes",url:"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK343617/",basis:"Describes morphology, beta-haemolysis and confirmatory identification tests"}],
  ["A raised C-reactive protein (CRP) result most directly indicates what?","C-reactive protein (CRP) बढेको नतिजाले मुख्यतः के जनाउँछ?",["Inflammation, but not its exact cause or location","A specific bacterial species","Definite rheumatoid arthritis","A confirmed viral infection only"],0,"CRP is an acute-phase protein produced by the liver in response to inflammation. A raised result is nonspecific and must be interpreted with symptoms, history and other tests.","CRP inflammation हुँदा liver ले बनाउने acute-phase protein हो। बढेको CRP nonspecific हुन्छ; लक्षण, इतिहास र अन्य परीक्षणसँगै व्याख्या गर्नुपर्छ।","Immunology",{status:"reviewed",source:"MedlinePlus — C-Reactive Protein Test",url:"https://medlineplus.gov/lab-tests/c-reactive-protein-crp-test/",basis:"Explains CRP rises with inflammation but cannot identify its cause or location"}]
 ];
 Q.push(...microbiologyReviewedBatch4); practiceQ.push(...microbiologyReviewedBatch4); mockQ.push(...microbiologyReviewedBatch4);

 // Immunology: immunoassays, serology and screening interpretation.
 const immunologyReviewedBatch1=[
  ["What is the basic principle of ELISA?","ELISA को आधारभूत सिद्धान्त के हो?",["Enzyme-labelled immunoreaction produces a measurable signal","Bacteria are counted under a microscope only","Red cells are separated by centrifugation","DNA is amplified by thermal cycling"],0,"ELISA uses specific antigen–antibody binding and an enzyme-labelled reagent. After substrate is added, an enzyme reaction produces a measurable signal, often a colour change.","ELISA मा specific antigen–antibody binding र enzyme-labelled reagent प्रयोग हुन्छ। Substrate थपेपछि enzyme reaction बाट मापन गर्न मिल्ने signal, प्रायः रङ परिवर्तन, आउँछ।","Immunology",{status:"reviewed",source:"NCBI MeSH — Enzyme-Linked Immunosorbent Assay",url:"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/68004797",basis:"Defines ELISA as an enzyme-labelled immunoassay with measurable signal"}],
  ["In an agglutination test, what visible reaction occurs when particulate antigens react with specific antibodies?","Agglutination test मा particulate antigen र specific antibody प्रतिक्रिया गर्दा कस्तो दृश्य परिवर्तन हुन्छ?",["Visible clumping","Gas production","Complete haemolysis in every case","DNA amplification"],0,"Agglutination is visible clumping caused by antibodies cross-linking particulate antigens such as cells or latex particles. Controls and the test method are essential for interpretation.","Agglutination भनेको antibody ले cell वा latex particle जस्ता particulate antigen लाई cross-link गर्दा देखिने clumping हो। सही व्याख्याका लागि control र test method आवश्यक हुन्छ।","Immunology",{status:"reviewed",source:"NCBI Bookshelf — Immunoassays and Agglutination",url:"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK562156/",basis:"General immunological principle of antigen-antibody binding and visible agglutination"}],
  ["Why is the Widal test alone not reliable for confirming acute typhoid fever?","Acute typhoid fever पुष्टि गर्न Widal test मात्र किन भरपर्दो हुँदैन?",["It may be positive from past exposure or vaccination and has false positives","It directly detects Salmonella DNA","It always identifies antibiotic resistance","It is a blood culture method"],0,"Widal measures antibodies and may not distinguish current infection from past exposure or vaccination. False positives occur; blood culture is the preferred diagnostic method for acute enteric fever.","Widal ले antibody मापन गर्छ; यसले हालको संक्रमणलाई पुरानो exposure वा vaccination बाट सधैँ छुट्याउन सक्दैन। False positive हुन सक्छ; acute enteric fever का लागि blood culture प्राथमिक विधि हो।","Immunology",{status:"reviewed",source:"CDC Yellow Book — Typhoid and Paratyphoid Fever",url:"https://www.cdc.gov/yellow-book/hcp/travel-associated-infections-diseases/typhoid-and-paratyphoid-fever.html",basis:"States Widal is unreliable and blood culture is preferred"}],
  ["A reactive VDRL or RPR result should generally be followed by which type of test for syphilis diagnosis?","VDRL वा RPR reactive आएपछि syphilis diagnosis का लागि सामान्यतया कुन प्रकारको test चाहिन्छ?",["A treponemal test","A urine glucose test","A platelet count","A blood grouping test"],0,"VDRL and RPR are nontreponemal tests. A presumptive serologic diagnosis requires both a nontreponemal and a treponemal test; one test type alone is insufficient.","VDRL र RPR nontreponemal test हुन्। Serologic diagnosis का लागि nontreponemal र treponemal दुवै प्रकारका test आवश्यक हुन्छन्; एउटा मात्र पर्याप्त हुँदैन।","Immunology",{status:"reviewed",source:"CDC — Syphilis STI Treatment Guidelines",url:"https://www.cdc.gov/std/treatment-guidelines/syphilis.htm",basis:"Requires both nontreponemal and treponemal serologic tests"}],
  ["A laboratory HIV antigen/antibody screening test is reactive. What is the correct interpretation?","Laboratory HIV antigen/antibody screening test reactive आयो। सही व्याख्या कुन हो?",["Preliminary reactive result requiring supplemental testing","HIV infection is confirmed by this result alone","The result proves HIV-2 only","No further testing is needed"],0,"A reactive initial HIV Ag/Ab screening result is not, by itself, a final diagnosis. Follow the validated national testing algorithm with supplemental testing; additional NAT may be needed for discordant results.","प्रारम्भिक HIV Ag/Ab screening reactive हुनु मात्र अन्तिम diagnosis होइन। राष्ट्रिय/मान्य testing algorithm अनुसार supplemental test गर्नुपर्छ; नमिलेका नतिजामा NAT आवश्यक पर्न सक्छ।","Immunology",{status:"reviewed",source:"CDC — HIV Testing",url:"https://www.cdc.gov/hivpartners/php/hiv-testing/index.html",basis:"Explains follow-up testing after reactive initial HIV screening"}],
  ["Which hepatitis B marker indicates current HBV infection in most clinical interpretations?","Hepatitis B को कुन marker ले धेरैजसो अवस्थामा हालको HBV infection जनाउँछ?",["HBsAg","Anti-HBs alone","Anti-HAV IgG","Anti-HCV"],0,"HBsAg indicates current HBV infection, acute or chronic, with rare exceptions such as transient positivity shortly after vaccination. Interpret it with anti-HBc and anti-HBs markers.","HBsAg ले सामान्यतया हालको HBV infection (acute वा chronic) जनाउँछ। Vaccination पछि केही समय transient positivity जस्ता अपवाद हुन सक्छन्। Anti-HBc र anti-HBs सँगै व्याख्या गर्नुपर्छ।","Immunology",{status:"reviewed",source:"CDC — Clinical Testing and Diagnosis for Hepatitis B",url:"https://www.cdc.gov/hepatitis-b/hcp/diagnosis-testing/",basis:"Defines HBsAg and recommends the HBV triple panel"}],
  ["A person has anti-HBs positive but total anti-HBc negative. What does this pattern usually indicate when vaccination is documented?","कुनै व्यक्तिमा anti-HBs positive र total anti-HBc negative छ। Vaccination भएको प्रमाण छ भने यसले सामान्यतया के जनाउँछ?",["Immunity due to hepatitis B vaccination","Acute hepatitis B infection","Chronic hepatitis B infection","Current hepatitis C infection"],0,"Anti-HBs without anti-HBc usually indicates vaccine-derived immunity when a completed hepatitis B vaccine series is documented. Natural infection generally produces anti-HBc.","Completed hepatitis B vaccine series को प्रमाण भएको अवस्थामा anti-HBs positive र anti-HBc negative हुनु vaccine बाट बनेको immunity सँग मिल्छ। प्राकृतिक संक्रमणमा सामान्यतया anti-HBc पनि देखिन्छ।","Immunology",{status:"reviewed",source:"CDC — Clinical Testing and Diagnosis for Hepatitis B",url:"https://www.cdc.gov/hepatitis-b/hcp/diagnosis-testing/",basis:"Explains anti-HBs and anti-HBc interpretation after vaccination versus infection"}]
 ];
 Q.push(...immunologyReviewedBatch1); practiceQ.push(...immunologyReviewedBatch1); mockQ.push(...immunologyReviewedBatch1);

 // Mycology, parasitology and virology: microscopy and molecular diagnosis.
 const microMycoParaViroBatch1=[
  ["What is the main purpose of adding 10% KOH to a skin scraping before microscopy?","Skin scraping लाई microscopy अघि 10% KOH थप्नुको मुख्य उद्देश्य के हो?",["To clear keratin and cellular debris so fungal elements can be seen","To stain bacteria purple","To culture viruses","To measure fungal susceptibility to antibiotics"],0,"KOH digests keratin and cellular debris, making fungal hyphae or yeast easier to see microscopically. It is a direct examination method, not a culture test.","KOH ले keratin र cellular debris हटाउन/clear गर्न मद्दत गर्छ, जसले fungal hyphae वा yeast microscope मा देख्न सजिलो बनाउँछ। यो direct examination हो, culture test होइन।","Mycology",{status:"reviewed",source:"CDC — Provider Performed Microscopy Procedures, KOH Procedure",url:"https://www.cdc.gov/lab-quality/media/pdfs/2025/07/PPMP_2025_Final-508c.pdf",basis:"Describes KOH digestion of specimen debris to visualize yeast and pseudohyphae"}],
  ["Which microscopic finding in a KOH preparation supports Candida infection?","KOH preparation मा कुन microscopic finding ले Candida infection लाई समर्थन गर्छ?",["Budding yeast with pseudohyphae","Acid-fast bacilli","Motile trophozoites with flagella only","Gram-negative diplococci"],0,"Candida may appear as budding yeast cells with pseudohyphae in a direct preparation. Microscopy must be interpreted with symptoms and, when indicated, culture or other tests because colonization can occur.","Candida direct preparation मा budding yeast र pseudohyphae का रूपमा देखिन सक्छ। Colonization पनि हुन सक्ने भएकाले microscopy लाई लक्षण र आवश्यक परे culture वा अन्य test सँगै व्याख्या गर्नुपर्छ।","Mycology",{status:"reviewed",source:"CDC — Provider Performed Microscopy Procedures, KOH Procedure",url:"https://www.cdc.gov/lab-quality/media/pdfs/2025/07/PPMP_2025_Final-508c.pdf",basis:"Illustrates budding yeast and pseudohyphae in KOH preparation"}],
  ["For malaria microscopy, which blood film is generally more sensitive for detecting low-density parasites?","Malaria microscopy मा कम parasite density पत्ता लगाउन कुन blood film बढी संवेदनशील हुन्छ?",["Thick blood film","Thin blood film","Peripheral smear without stain","Serum film"],0,"A thick film concentrates parasites from a larger blood volume and is more sensitive for detection. A thin film is better for species identification and estimating parasitemia.","Thick film मा धेरै रगतको parasite सानो क्षेत्रमा concentrate हुन्छ, त्यसैले detection बढी संवेदनशील हुन्छ। Thin film species पहिचान र parasitemia अनुमान गर्न उपयोगी हुन्छ।","Parasitology",{status:"reviewed",source:"CDC — Evaluation and Diagnosis of Malaria",url:"https://www.cdc.gov/malaria/hcp/clinical-guidance/evaluation-diagnosis.html",basis:"States thick smears are more sensitive and thin smears aid species identification"}],
  ["Which stain is recommended by WHO for routine malaria microscopy?","WHO ले routine malaria microscopy का लागि कुन stain सिफारिस गर्छ?",["Giemsa stain","India ink","Albert stain","Lactophenol cotton blue"],0,"Giemsa is the recommended stain for malaria microscopy. Both thick and thin films from the same patient should be examined for detection and species assessment.","Malaria microscopy का लागि Giemsa stain सिफारिस गरिन्छ। Detection र species assessment का लागि एउटै बिरामीको thick र thin दुवै film जाँच्नुपर्छ।","Parasitology",{status:"reviewed",source:"WHO — Malaria Microscopy",url:"https://www.who.int/teams/global-malaria-programme/case-management/diagnosis/microscopy",basis:"Recommends Giemsa and examination of both thick and thin films"}],
  ["In malaria diagnosis, what is the main advantage of a thin blood film?","Malaria diagnosis मा thin blood film को मुख्य फाइदा के हो?",["Better Plasmodium species identification and parasite quantification","It always detects more parasites than a thick film","It detects antibodies only","It replaces clinical assessment"],0,"Thin films preserve red-cell morphology and help identify Plasmodium species and quantify parasitemia. Thick films are generally more sensitive for initial parasite detection.","Thin film ले RBC को morphology जोगाउँछ र Plasmodium species पहिचान तथा parasitemia quantification मा मद्दत गर्छ। प्रारम्भिक parasite detection का लागि thick film सामान्यतया बढी संवेदनशील हुन्छ।","Parasitology",{status:"reviewed",source:"CDC — Malaria Diagnostic Tests",url:"https://www.cdc.gov/malaria/hcp/diagnosis-testing/malaria-diagnostic-tests.html",basis:"Explains complementary roles of thick and thin smears"}],
  ["Which molecular method is commonly used to detect influenza viral RNA in respiratory specimens?","Respiratory specimen मा influenza viral RNA पत्ता लगाउन सामान्यतया कुन molecular method प्रयोग हुन्छ?",["RT-PCR","Widal test","VDRL","Gram staining"],0,"RT-PCR and other nucleic acid amplification tests detect influenza viral RNA in respiratory specimens with high sensitivity and specificity. A positive molecular result does not necessarily prove viable virus is present.","RT-PCR तथा अन्य nucleic acid amplification test ले respiratory specimen मा influenza viral RNA पत्ता लगाउँछन्। Positive molecular result ले viable virus नै छ भनेर अनिवार्य रूपमा प्रमाणित गर्दैन।","Virology",{status:"reviewed",source:"CDC — Molecular Assays for Diagnosis of Influenza Virus Infection",url:"https://www.cdc.gov/flu/hcp/testing-methods/molecular-assays.html",basis:"Describes RT-PCR and NAAT detection of influenza viral RNA"}],
  ["Why should a respiratory specimen for viral molecular testing be collected and transported according to the test kit instructions?","Viral molecular testing का लागि respiratory specimen kit को निर्देशनअनुसार संकलन र transport किन गर्नुपर्छ?",["To preserve specimen quality and nucleic acid for reliable testing","To make all viruses grow on bacterial agar","To convert RNA into antibodies","To avoid patient identification"],0,"Specimen type, collection technique, transport medium, temperature and timing are assay-specific. Incorrect handling can reduce nucleic-acid quality and cause invalid or false-negative results; follow the validated assay instructions.","Specimen type, collection technique, transport medium, temperature र timing assay अनुसार फरक हुन्छ। गलत handling ले nucleic acid को गुणस्तर घटाएर invalid वा false-negative नतिजा दिन सक्छ; validated assay instruction पालना गर्नुपर्छ।","Virology",{status:"reviewed",source:"CDC — Molecular Assays for Diagnosis of Influenza Virus Infection",url:"https://www.cdc.gov/flu/hcp/testing-methods/molecular-assays.html",basis:"Provides respiratory specimen and molecular assay guidance"}]
 ];
 Q.push(...microMycoParaViroBatch1); practiceQ.push(...microMycoParaViroBatch1); mockQ.push(...microMycoParaViroBatch1);











  const biochemistryAdvancedQCBatch1 = [
   ["A control has mean 100 mg/dL and SD 2 mg/dL. Today's value is 105 mg/dL. How many SDs above the mean is it?","Control को mean 100 mg/dL र SD 2 mg/dL छ। आजको value 105 mg/dL आयो। Mean भन्दा कति SD माथि छ?",["1 SD","2 SD","2.5 SD","5 SD"],2,"Z-score = (105 − 100) / 2 = +2.5 SD. This is beyond +2 SD and must be assessed using the laboratory's QC rules.","Z-score = (105 − 100) / 2 = +2.5 SD हुन्छ। यो +2 SD भन्दा बाहिर भएकाले प्रयोगशालाको QC rule अनुसार मूल्याङ्कन गर्नुपर्छ।","Clinical Biochemistry & QC",{status:"reviewed",source:"WHO — Laboratory Quality Management System Handbook, Section 7.5",url:"https://iris.who.int/bitstream/handle/10665/44665/9789241548274_eng.pdf?sequence=1",basis:"Explains control means, SD limits and Levey–Jennings charts"}],
   ["One control result exceeds +3 SD. Which Westgard rule is violated?","एउटा control result +3 SD भन्दा माथि छ। कुन Westgard rule उल्लङ्घन हुन्छ?",["1-2s","1-3s","2-2s","R-4s"],1,"The 1-3s rule is violated when one control measurement exceeds the mean by more than 3 SD; reject and investigate the run.","एउटा control measurement mean बाट 3 SD भन्दा बढी टाढा भए 1-3s rule उल्लङ्घन हुन्छ; run reject गरी जाँच गर्नुपर्छ।","Clinical Biochemistry & QC",{status:"reviewed",source:"WHO — Laboratory Quality Management System Handbook, Section 7.5",url:"https://iris.who.int/bitstream/handle/10665/44665/9789241548274_eng.pdf?sequence=1",basis:"Describes Levey–Jennings limits and Westgard multirules"}],
   ["Two consecutive control results from the same level are both above +2 SD. Which rule is suggested?","एउटै control level का लगातार दुई result +2 SD माथि छन्। कुन rule संकेत हुन्छ?",["1-2s","2-2s","R-4s","10x"],1,"The 2-2s rule is triggered when two consecutive control results exceed the same +2 SD limit (or same −2 SD limit), suggesting systematic error.","लगातार दुई control result एउटै दिशाको +2 SD (वा −2 SD) सीमा बाहिर भए 2-2s rule लाग्छ र systematic error संकेत हुन सक्छ।","Clinical Biochemistry & QC",{status:"reviewed",source:"WHO — Laboratory Quality Management System Handbook, Section 7.5",url:"https://iris.who.int/bitstream/handle/10665/44665/9789241548274_eng.pdf?sequence=1",basis:"Describes Westgard multirule system"}],
   ["A single control value is +2.2 SD and 1-2s is used as a warning rule. What is the best interpretation?","एउटा control value +2.2 SD छ र 1-2s warning rule हो। सही व्याख्या के हो?",["Always accept without review","Treat as warning; inspect other QC rules","Report all patient results immediately","Change the target mean"],1,"A single result beyond ±2 SD is a warning under 1-2s, not necessarily an automatic rejection by itself. Review the complete QC pattern and validated laboratory rules.","एकल result ±2 SD बाहिर हुनु 1-2s warning हो, आफैँमा सधैँ automatic rejection होइन। सम्पूर्ण QC pattern र validated rule हेर्नुपर्छ।","Clinical Biochemistry & QC",{status:"reviewed",source:"WHO — Laboratory Quality Management System Handbook, Section 7.5",url:"https://iris.who.int/bitstream/handle/10665/44665/9789241548274_eng.pdf?sequence=1",basis:"Explains control limits and multirule QC"}],
   ["A visibly hemolyzed serum has unexpectedly high potassium. What is the likely cause?","Hemolyzed serum मा potassium असामान्य रूपमा उच्च छ। सम्भावित कारण के हो?",["Potassium release from red cells","Platelet clumping lowers potassium","Bilirubin increases potassium","No interference is possible"],0,"Hemolysis releases intracellular potassium from red cells and may falsely increase measured potassium. Assess sample acceptability and follow method-specific policy; recollection may be required.","Hemolysis हुँदा RBC भित्रको potassium बाहिर निस्केर measured potassium झूटो रूपमा बढ्न सक्छ। Sample acceptability र method-specific policy हेर्नुपर्छ; आवश्यक परे पुनः नमुना लिनुपर्छ।","Clinical Biochemistry & QC",{status:"reviewed",source:"Consensus Statement for the Management and Reporting of Haemolysed Specimens",url:"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5242477/",basis:"Explains potassium release and haemolysis-related interference"}],
   ["A markedly lipemic sample causes an unexpected photometric result. What is the likely mechanism?","धेरै lipemic sample बाट photometric test मा अनपेक्षित result आयो। सम्भावित mechanism के हो?",["Light scattering from turbidity","Bacterial growth in cuvette","Serum becomes plasma","All electrolytes disappear"],0,"Lipemia causes turbidity and light scattering that can interfere with photometric assays. The effect is assay-dependent; follow analyzer and reagent instructions.","Lipemia ले turbidity र light scattering गराउँछ, जसले photometric assay मा असर गर्न सक्छ। प्रभाव assay अनुसार फरक हुन्छ; analyzer र reagent निर्देशन पालना गर्नुपर्छ।","Clinical Biochemistry & QC",{status:"reviewed",source:"CDC — Potential Sources of Error: Hemolysis, Hyperbilirubinemia and Lipemia",url:"https://stacks.cdc.gov/view/cdc/53206/cdc_53206_DS1.pdf",basis:"Describes lipemic turbidity and potential measurement interference"}],
   ["Glucose control target is 120 mg/dL and measured value is 108 mg/dL. What is percentage bias?","Glucose control target 120 mg/dL र measured value 108 mg/dL छ। Percentage bias कति हो?",["−5%","−10%","+10%","−12%"],1,"Percentage bias = (measured − target) / target × 100 = (108 − 120) / 120 × 100 = −10%.","Percentage bias = (measured − target) / target × 100 = (108 − 120) / 120 × 100 = −10% हुन्छ।","Clinical Biochemistry & QC",{status:"reviewed",source:"WHO — Laboratory Quality Management System Handbook",url:"https://iris.who.int/bitstream/handle/10665/44665/9789241548274_eng.pdf?sequence=1",basis:"Covers accuracy and quantitative quality assessment"}],
   ["Repeated control results are close to one another but consistently far from the assigned target. This indicates:","Control result हरू एकअर्कासँग नजिक छन् तर assigned target बाट लगातार टाढा छन्। यसले के जनाउँछ?",["Good precision, poor accuracy","Poor precision, good accuracy","Perfect accuracy and precision","No analytical issue"],0,"Close results indicate good precision; consistent deviation from target indicates bias and poor accuracy.","नतिजा एकअर्कासँग नजिक हुनु good precision हो; target बाट लगातार टाढा हुनु bias अर्थात् poor accuracy हो।","Clinical Biochemistry & QC",{status:"reviewed",source:"WHO — Laboratory Quality Management System Handbook",url:"https://iris.who.int/bitstream/handle/10665/44665/9789241548274_eng.pdf?sequence=1",basis:"Defines accuracy and precision in laboratory quality management"}],
   ["Internal QC is outside the acceptable range before patient reporting. What should be done?","Patient report गर्नुअघि internal QC acceptable range बाहिर आयो। के गर्नुपर्छ?",["Release all results","Hold affected results and investigate QC failure","Delete the QC record","Manually adjust patient values"],1,"Do not release affected results until the analytical system is demonstrated to be in control. Investigate, correct the cause, rerun controls and follow SOP before reporting.","Analytical system control मा छ भन्ने पुष्टि नभएसम्म प्रभावित result release गर्नु हुँदैन। कारण जाँच्ने, corrective action गर्ने, control फेरि चलाउने र SOP पालना गरेपछि report गर्नुपर्छ।","Clinical Biochemistry & QC",{status:"reviewed",source:"WHO — Laboratory Quality Management System Handbook, Section 7.5",url:"https://iris.who.int/bitstream/handle/10665/44665/9789241548274_eng.pdf?sequence=1",basis:"Out-of-control runs must be rejected and investigated before patient results are released"}],
   ["Control values gradually move upward over several days while remaining within limits. What is this pattern called?","Control value धेरै दिनसम्म बिस्तारै माथितिर सर्दै गएको छ तर limits भित्र छ। यसलाई के भनिन्छ?",["Trend","Random error only","Clerical error","Reference interval"],0,"A trend is a gradual, sustained movement in one direction. It may indicate developing systematic error and should be investigated.","Trend भनेको control value क्रमशः एउटै दिशातिर सर्दै जानु हो। यसले developing systematic error संकेत गर्न सक्छ र जाँच गर्नुपर्छ।","Clinical Biochemistry & QC",{status:"reviewed",source:"WHO — Laboratory Quality Management System Handbook, Section 7.5",url:"https://iris.who.int/bitstream/handle/10665/44665/9789241548274_eng.pdf?sequence=1",basis:"Explains plotting and interpretation of QC values over time"}]
  ];

  const biochemistryNumericalBatch1 = [
   ["A serum sample is diluted by mixing 1 mL sample with 9 mL diluent. What is the final dilution?","Serum sample 1 mL र diluent 9 mL मिसाइयो। Final dilution कति हुन्छ?",["1:5","1:9","1:10","1:11"],2,"Total volume = 1 + 9 = 10 mL. The sample is 1 part in 10 total parts, so the dilution is 1:10.","Total volume = 1 + 9 = 10 mL हुन्छ। जम्मा १० भागमध्ये sample १ भाग भएकाले dilution 1:10 हो।","Clinical Biochemistry Calculations",{status:"reviewed",source:"Association for Laboratory Medicine — Calculations in Laboratory Science",url:"https://labmed.org.uk/static/61acfe35-c95f-49a5-815f627866a2e0e4/Calculations-in-Laboratory-Science.pdf",basis:"Explains sample-to-final-volume dilution calculations"}],
   ["A 1:10 diluted sample gives a glucose result of 18 mg/dL. What is the estimated original concentration?","1:10 diluted sample मा glucose 18 mg/dL आयो। Original concentration कति हुन्छ?",["18 mg/dL","90 mg/dL","180 mg/dL","1,800 mg/dL"],2,"Original concentration = measured diluted concentration × dilution factor = 18 × 10 = 180 mg/dL. Apply the factor only when the dilution was prepared and validated correctly.","Original concentration = diluted result × dilution factor = 18 × 10 = 180 mg/dL हुन्छ। Dilution सही तरिकाले तयार र validate भएको अवस्थामा मात्र factor लगाउनुपर्छ।","Clinical Biochemistry Calculations",{status:"reviewed",source:"Association for Laboratory Medicine — Calculations in Laboratory Science",url:"https://labmed.org.uk/static/61acfe35-c95f-49a5-815f627866a2e0e4/Calculations-in-Laboratory-Science.pdf",basis:"Shows how to calculate original concentration after sample dilution"}],
   ["How much stock solution is needed to prepare 100 mL of a 1:20 dilution?","1:20 dilution को 100 mL solution बनाउन stock solution कति चाहिन्छ?",["2 mL","5 mL","10 mL","20 mL"],1,"Stock volume = final volume / dilution factor = 100 / 20 = 5 mL. Add diluent to make the final volume 100 mL (95 mL diluent).","Stock volume = final volume / dilution factor = 100 / 20 = 5 mL हुन्छ। Final volume 100 mL पुर्‍याउन 95 mL diluent थपिन्छ।","Clinical Biochemistry Calculations",{status:"reviewed",source:"University of Auckland — Laboratory Calculations",url:"https://www.fmhs.auckland.ac.nz/assets/fmhs/sms/pharmacology/teaching/medsci204/docs/lab11.pdf",basis:"Explains dilution preparation and stock-volume calculation"}],
   ["A reagent contains 2 g solute in a final volume of 100 mL. What is its concentration in % w/v?","Reagent को final volume 100 mL मा 2 g solute छ। यसको % w/v concentration कति हो?",["0.2%","1%","2%","20%"],2,"% w/v means grams of solute per 100 mL of final solution. Therefore, 2 g in 100 mL = 2% w/v.","% w/v भनेको 100 mL final solution मा भएको solute को gram हो। त्यसैले 100 mL मा 2 g = 2% w/v हुन्छ।","Clinical Biochemistry Calculations",{status:"reviewed",source:"Clinical Chemistry: A Laboratory Perspective — Summary of Calculations",url:"https://uodiyala.edu.iq/uploads/PDF%20ELIBRARY%20UODIYALA/EL27/3uodiyala%20Arneson_Clinical%20Chemistry-A%20Laboratory%20Perspective.pdf",basis:"Lists % w/v as grams per 100 mL"}],
   ["A solution contains 0.5 mol solute in 1 litre. What is its molarity?","१ litre solution मा 0.5 mol solute छ। यसको molarity कति हो?",["0.05 M","0.5 M","1 M","5 M"],1,"Molarity = moles of solute / litres of solution = 0.5 / 1 = 0.5 mol/L or 0.5 M.","Molarity = solute को mole / solution को litre = 0.5 / 1 = 0.5 mol/L अर्थात् 0.5 M हुन्छ।","Clinical Biochemistry Calculations",{status:"reviewed",source:"University of Auckland — Laboratory Calculations",url:"https://www.fmhs.auckland.ac.nz/assets/fmhs/sms/pharmacology/teaching/medsci204/docs/lab11.pdf",basis:"Defines molar concentration and SI prefixes"}],
   ["Convert 2.5 mmol/L glucose to mg/dL. Use molecular mass 180 g/mol.","2.5 mmol/L glucose लाई mg/dL मा बदल्नुहोस्। Molecular mass 180 g/mol प्रयोग गर्नुहोस्।",["4.5 mg/dL","45 mg/dL","90 mg/dL","450 mg/dL"],1,"For glucose, mg/dL = mmol/L × 18. Thus 2.5 × 18 = 45 mg/dL. The factor follows from glucose molecular mass and unit conversion.","Glucose का लागि mg/dL = mmol/L × 18 हुन्छ। त्यसैले 2.5 × 18 = 45 mg/dL। यो factor glucose को molecular mass र unit conversion बाट आउँछ।","Clinical Biochemistry Calculations",{status:"reviewed",source:"Clinical Chemistry: A Laboratory Perspective — Summary of Calculations",url:"https://uodiyala.edu.iq/uploads/PDF%20ELIBRARY%20UODIYALA/EL27/3uodiyala%20Arneson_Clinical%20Chemistry-A%20Laboratory%20Perspective.pdf",basis:"Provides molecular-weight-based conversion between mass and molar concentration"}],
   ["A spectrophotometric glucose assay gives absorbance 0.40 for the patient and 0.20 for a 100 mg/dL standard. What is the patient glucose concentration?","Spectrophotometric glucose assay मा patient absorbance 0.40 र 100 mg/dL standard को absorbance 0.20 छ। Patient glucose कति हो?",["50 mg/dL","100 mg/dL","200 mg/dL","400 mg/dL"],2,"Assuming a linear assay and appropriate blanking: concentration = (A patient / A standard) × standard concentration = (0.40 / 0.20) × 100 = 200 mg/dL.","Assay linear र blanking सही भएको अवस्थामा concentration = (A patient / A standard) × standard concentration = (0.40 / 0.20) × 100 = 200 mg/dL हुन्छ।","Clinical Biochemistry Calculations",{status:"reviewed",source:"Clinical Chemistry: A Laboratory Perspective — Summary of Calculations",url:"https://uodiyala.edu.iq/uploads/PDF%20ELIBRARY%20UODIYALA/EL27/3uodiyala%20Arneson_Clinical%20Chemistry-A%20Laboratory%20Perspective.pdf",basis:"Lists the standard-to-unknown absorbance calculation for spectrophotometry"}],
   ["Convert 750 microlitres (µL) to millilitres (mL).","750 microlitre (µL) लाई millilitre (mL) मा बदल्नुहोस्।",["0.075 mL","0.75 mL","7.5 mL","75 mL"],1,"1,000 µL = 1 mL. Therefore, 750 µL / 1,000 = 0.75 mL.","1,000 µL = 1 mL हुन्छ। त्यसैले 750 µL / 1,000 = 0.75 mL हुन्छ।","Clinical Biochemistry Calculations",{status:"reviewed",source:"University of Auckland — Laboratory Calculations",url:"https://www.fmhs.auckland.ac.nz/assets/fmhs/sms/pharmacology/teaching/medsci204/docs/lab11.pdf",basis:"Lists metric prefixes and volume conversions"}],
   ["A 1:5 dilution is followed by a 1:4 dilution. What is the overall dilution factor?","1:5 dilution पछि 1:4 dilution गरियो। Overall dilution factor कति हुन्छ?",["5","9","20","25"],2,"For serial dilutions, multiply the individual dilution factors: 5 × 4 = 20. The overall dilution is 1:20.","Serial dilution मा प्रत्येक चरणको dilution factor गुणन गरिन्छ: 5 × 4 = 20। Overall dilution 1:20 हुन्छ।","Clinical Biochemistry Calculations",{status:"reviewed",source:"Linné & Ringsrud's Clinical Laboratory Science — Laboratory Mathematics and Solution Preparation",url:"https://e-library.nu.edu.sd/pdfs/1VmFmk2pznND5Yzkt0KZcUbypUSWoD1RA.pdf",basis:"Explains serial dilution and multiplication of dilution factors"}],
   ["A solution is made by dissolving 4 g of solute and making the final volume up to 200 mL. What is the concentration in % w/v?","4 g solute घोलेर final volume 200 mL बनाइयो। Concentration % w/v कति हुन्छ?",["1%","2%","4%","8%"],1,"% w/v = grams per 100 mL. 4 g in 200 mL is equivalent to 2 g in 100 mL, so the concentration is 2% w/v.","% w/v = प्रति 100 mL मा gram हो। 200 mL मा 4 g भनेको 100 mL मा 2 g बराबर हो, त्यसैले 2% w/v हुन्छ।","Clinical Biochemistry Calculations",{status:"reviewed",source:"Clinical Chemistry: A Laboratory Perspective — Summary of Calculations",url:"https://uodiyala.edu.iq/uploads/PDF%20ELIBRARY%20UODIYALA/EL27/3uodiyala%20Arneson_Clinical%20Chemistry-A%20Laboratory%20Perspective.pdf",basis:"Lists % w/v concentration calculations"}]
  ];

  const microbiologyAdvancedCaseBatch1 = [
   ["A pure bacterial isolate is tested by Kirby–Bauer disk diffusion. Which measurement is used to interpret susceptibility?","Pure bacterial isolate मा Kirby–Bauer disk diffusion गरियो। Susceptibility व्याख्या गर्न कुन measurement प्रयोग हुन्छ?",["Colony colour only","Diameter of inhibition zone","Number of colonies on blood agar only","Gram reaction alone"],1,"The diameter of the inhibition zone is measured in millimetres and interpreted using current organism- and drug-specific breakpoint tables and the method standard used by the laboratory.","Inhibition zone को diameter millimetre मा नापिन्छ र laboratory ले अपनाएको current organism- र drug-specific breakpoint table अनुसार interpretation गरिन्छ।","Clinical Microbiology & AST",{status:"reviewed",source:"EUCAST — Disk Diffusion and Quality Control",url:"https://www.eucast.org/bacteria/methodology-and-instructions/disk-diffusion-and-quality-control/",basis:"Describes standardized disk diffusion and breakpoint-based interpretation"}],
   ["An isolate has an MIC of 2 mg/L for a particular antibiotic. What does MIC represent?","कुनै antibiotic का लागि isolate को MIC 2 mg/L छ। MIC ले के जनाउँछ?",["Highest concentration allowing growth","Lowest concentration inhibiting visible growth under defined test conditions","Drug concentration in the patient's blood","Diameter of inhibition zone"],1,"MIC is the lowest antimicrobial concentration that prevents visible growth under defined in-vitro test conditions. Clinical S/I/R categorization requires the relevant current breakpoint.","MIC भनेको निर्धारित in-vitro test condition मा visible growth रोक्ने सबैभन्दा कम antimicrobial concentration हो। Clinical S/I/R वर्गीकरणका लागि सम्बन्धित current breakpoint चाहिन्छ।","Clinical Microbiology & AST",{status:"reviewed",source:"EUCAST — Disk Diffusion and Quality Control",url:"https://www.eucast.org/bacteria/methodology-and-instructions/disk-diffusion-and-quality-control/",basis:"Identifies MIC as the basis of susceptibility testing and clinical breakpoints"}],
   ["A technologist measures a 22-mm inhibition zone but has no current breakpoint table for the organism–drug pair. What is the safest action?","Technologist ले 22-mm inhibition zone नाप्यो तर organism–drug pair को current breakpoint table छैन। सुरक्षित कदम के हो?",["Call it susceptible using a universal 20-mm rule","Interpret using a current validated standard or refer for review; do not guess","Report resistant for every isolate","Ignore organism identity"],1,"Zone diameters cannot be interpreted with one universal cutoff. Use current validated CLSI or EUCAST criteria for the correct organism, antimicrobial, method and disk content.","Zone diameter का लागि एउटै universal cutoff हुँदैन। सही organism, antimicrobial, method र disk content का लागि current validated CLSI वा EUCAST criteria प्रयोग गर्नुपर्छ।","Clinical Microbiology & AST",{status:"reviewed",source:"EUCAST — Disk Diffusion and Quality Control; CLSI — Breakpoint Implementation Toolkit",url:"https://www.eucast.org/bacteria/methodology-and-instructions/disk-diffusion-and-quality-control/",basis:"Requires standardized methods and current clinical breakpoints"}],
   ["A Staphylococcus aureus isolate is suspected to be MRSA. Which disk is commonly used in phenotypic disk-diffusion testing?","Staphylococcus aureus isolate मा MRSA शंका छ। Phenotypic disk-diffusion testing मा सामान्यतया कुन disk प्रयोग गरिन्छ?",["Cefoxitin","Metronidazole","Vancomycin","Colistin"],0,"Cefoxitin disk diffusion is a recommended phenotypic method for detecting methicillin resistance in S. aureus; interpretation must follow the current standard and species-specific criteria.","S. aureus मा methicillin resistance पत्ता लगाउन cefoxitin disk diffusion सिफारिस गरिएको phenotypic method हो। Interpretation current standard र species-specific criteria अनुसार गर्नुपर्छ।","Clinical Microbiology & AST",{status:"reviewed",source:"CDC — Laboratory Testing for Methicillin (oxacillin)-resistant Staphylococcus aureus",url:"https://www.cdc.gov/mrsa/php/laboratories/",basis:"Lists cefoxitin disk diffusion among recommended phenotypic MRSA tests"}],
   ["A blood culture is ordered for a patient with suspected bloodstream infection. When should it ideally be collected relative to antimicrobial therapy?","Bloodstream infection शंका भएको बिरामीको blood culture मागिएको छ। Antimicrobial therapy सँग तुलना गर्दा कहिले संकलन गर्नु उपयुक्त हुन्छ?",["After several antibiotic doses","Before antimicrobial therapy, if possible","Only after fever resolves","At any time without documentation"],1,"Blood cultures should be collected before antimicrobial therapy when possible, because prior treatment can reduce recovery of bloodstream pathogens. Do not delay urgent treatment when clinically unsafe.","सम्भव भए antimicrobial therapy सुरु गर्नुअघि blood culture लिनुपर्छ, किनकि पहिले औषधि दिँदा pathogen recovery घट्न सक्छ। उपचार ढिलाइ गर्नु जोखिमपूर्ण भए urgent treatment रोक्नु हुँदैन।","Clinical Microbiology & Specimen Collection",{status:"reviewed",source:"CDC — Collect Adult Blood Culture Sets",url:"https://www.cdc.gov/lab-quality/php/preventing-adult-blood-culture-contamination/collect.html",basis:"Recommends collecting blood cultures before antimicrobial administration if possible"}],
   ["For an adult with suspected bloodstream infection, what is the usual composition of one conventional blood culture set?","Bloodstream infection शंका भएको adult मा एउटा conventional blood culture set मा सामान्यतया के हुन्छ?",["One urine bottle","One aerobic and one anaerobic bottle","Two fungal plates","One serum separator tube"],1,"A conventional adult blood culture set generally consists of an aerobic and an anaerobic bottle. Follow the specific blood culture system and institutional SOP.","Adult को conventional blood culture set मा सामान्यतया एउटा aerobic र एउटा anaerobic bottle हुन्छ। सम्बन्धित blood culture system र संस्थाको SOP पालना गर्नुपर्छ।","Clinical Microbiology & Specimen Collection",{status:"reviewed",source:"CDC — Collect Adult Blood Culture Sets",url:"https://www.cdc.gov/lab-quality/php/preventing-adult-blood-culture-contamination/collect.html",basis:"Specifies aerobic and anaerobic bottles in a conventional blood culture set"}],
   ["A blood culture bottle is received with no patient identifiers. What should the laboratory do?","Patient identifier नभएको blood culture bottle प्रयोगशालामा आयो। प्रयोगशालाले के गर्नुपर्छ?",["Guess the patient's identity","Follow specimen rejection and recollection policy; never guess identity","Label it with the ward name only","Process it as an anonymous sample"],1,"Positive specimen identification and integrity must be maintained. An unlabeled or inadequately identified specimen should be managed according to the laboratory's documented rejection and recollection policy.","Specimen को सही पहिचान र integrity कायम हुनुपर्छ। Label नभएको वा अपर्याप्त पहिचान भएको नमुना laboratory को documented rejection र recollection policy अनुसार व्यवस्थापन गर्नुपर्छ।","Clinical Microbiology & Specimen Collection",{status:"reviewed",source:"CDC — Collect Adult Blood Culture Sets",url:"https://www.cdc.gov/lab-quality/php/preventing-adult-blood-culture-contamination/collect.html",basis:"Requires unique patient identifiers and written specimen identification procedures"}],
   ["A urine culture specimen cannot reach the laboratory within two hours at room temperature. What is a common acceptable preservation approach?","Urine culture specimen room temperature मा दुई घण्टाभित्र प्रयोगशाला पुग्न सक्दैन। सामान्यतया कुन preservation उपाय अपनाउन सकिन्छ?",["Keep it warm near a heater","Refrigerate at 2–8°C or use a validated preservative system","Leave it open to air","Add household disinfectant"],1,"If prompt processing is not possible, refrigeration at 2–8°C or a validated boric-acid transport system can help preserve urine culture quality. Follow the laboratory's validated specimen requirements.","तुरुन्त processing सम्भव नभए 2–8°C मा refrigeration वा validated boric-acid transport system ले urine culture को गुणस्तर जोगाउन मद्दत गर्छ। Laboratory को validated specimen requirement पालना गर्नुपर्छ।","Clinical Microbiology & Specimen Collection",{status:"reviewed",source:"NCBI Bookshelf — Urine Culture: Clinical Use and Interpretation",url:"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK557569/",basis:"Describes timely urine culture processing, refrigeration and boric-acid preservation"}],
   ["A urine specimen remains unpreserved at room temperature for many hours before culture. What is the main concern?","Urine specimen preservation नगरी room temperature मा धेरै घण्टा राखेर culture गरियो। मुख्य समस्या के हुन सक्छ?",["Bacterial multiplication may distort colony counts","All bacteria immediately die","Urine becomes sterile","Only red cells multiply"],0,"Bacteria can multiply in unpreserved urine held at room temperature, potentially increasing colony counts and compromising interpretation. Follow validated transport time and preservation procedures.","Room temperature मा preservation नगरी राखिएको urine मा bacteria बढ्न सक्छन्, जसले colony count बढाएर interpretation बिगार्न सक्छ। Validated transport time र preservation procedure पालना गर्नुपर्छ।","Clinical Microbiology & Specimen Collection",{status:"reviewed",source:"NCBI Bookshelf — Urine Culture: Clinical Use and Interpretation",url:"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK557569/",basis:"Explains bacterial overgrowth and deterioration in delayed unpreserved urine specimens"}],
   ["A laboratory's antimicrobial susceptibility QC strain gives an out-of-range result. What should be done before reporting patient AST results?","Laboratory को antimicrobial susceptibility QC strain को result range बाहिर आयो। Patient AST result report गर्नुअघि के गर्नुपर्छ?",["Ignore QC if patient isolate grows well","Investigate the QC failure and resolve it according to SOP before releasing affected results","Change the patient's organism name","Use an old breakpoint without review"],1,"AST quality control verifies that the test system performs as expected. An out-of-range QC result requires investigation and corrective action under the laboratory SOP; affected patient results should not be released until validity is established.","AST quality control ले test system अपेक्षित रूपमा चलेको छ कि छैन जाँच्छ। QC result range बाहिर आए SOP अनुसार कारण जाँच र corrective action गर्नुपर्छ; validity पुष्टि नभएसम्म प्रभावित patient result release गर्नु हुँदैन।","Clinical Microbiology & AST Quality",{status:"reviewed",source:"EUCAST — Disk Diffusion and Quality Control",url:"https://www.eucast.org/bacteria/methodology-and-instructions/disk-diffusion-and-quality-control/",basis:"Provides standardized AST quality-control procedures and documents"}]
  ];
  
 const bloodBankAdvancedCaseBatch1 = [
  ["Forward and reverse ABO grouping results do not agree in a patient awaiting red-cell transfusion. What should the laboratory do first?","Red-cell transfusion पर्खिरहेको बिरामीको forward र reverse ABO grouping मिलेन। प्रयोगशालाले पहिले के गर्नुपर्छ?",["Choose the stronger reaction and issue blood","Resolve the discrepancy before routine red-cell issue; repeat/investigate and verify identity","Report group AB automatically","Ignore reverse grouping"],1,"ABO grouping discrepancies must be investigated and resolved before routine red-cell issue. Check patient/sample identity, repeat testing and seek senior/reference-laboratory support as required. If transfusion is urgently required before resolution, follow the emergency-release policy, commonly using group O red cells.","ABO grouping नमिलेमा नियमित red-cell issue गर्नु अघि discrepancy समाधान गर्नुपर्छ। बिरामी/नमुना पहिचान जाँच्ने, परीक्षण दोहोर्‍याउने र आवश्यक परे senior वा reference laboratory को सहयोग लिने। तुरुन्त रगत चाहिएको अवस्थामा emergency-release policy पालना गर्ने, जसमा प्रायः group O red cells प्रयोग हुन्छन्।","Blood Banking & Compatibility",{status:"reviewed",source:"Guidelines for pre-transfusion compatibility procedures; NCBI Bookshelf — Pretransfusion Testing",url:"https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1111/j.1365-3148.2012.01199.x",basis:"ABO grouping anomalies must be resolved before red-cell issue; emergency group O may be used under policy"}],
  ["A patient's antibody screen detects a clinically significant anti-K antibody. Which red-cell unit should be selected?","बिरामीको antibody screen मा clinically significant anti-K भेटियो। कुन red-cell unit छान्नुपर्छ?",["K-antigen-positive unit","K-antigen-negative unit that is crossmatch compatible","Any ABO-compatible unit without further testing","Only group AB red cells"],1,"When a clinically significant red-cell antibody is identified, select donor red cells lacking the corresponding antigen and confirm compatibility by the appropriate crossmatch method.","Clinically significant red-cell antibody भेटिएमा सम्बन्धित antigen नभएको donor red cell छान्नुपर्छ र उपयुक्त crossmatch बाट compatible भएको पुष्टि गर्नुपर्छ।","Blood Banking & Compatibility",{status:"reviewed",source:"Indian National Blood Transfusion Council — Standards for Blood Banks & Blood Transfusion Services",url:"https://cdnbbsr.s3waas.gov.in/s31177967c7957072da3dc1db4ceb30e7a/uploads/2023/01/2023011812.pdf",basis:"Requires antigen-negative compatible red cells when clinically significant antibodies are detected"}],
  ["A recipient's major crossmatch shows agglutination. How should the tested donor red-cell unit be interpreted?","बिरामीको major crossmatch मा agglutination देखियो। परीक्षण गरिएको donor red-cell unit लाई कसरी बुझ्ने?",["Compatible; issue immediately","Incompatible; do not issue until investigated and a compatible unit is found","Compatible if the donor is group O","Ignore the reaction if the sample is clear"],1,"Agglutination in the major crossmatch indicates serologic incompatibility in the test system. Do not issue that unit as compatible; investigate the cause and select a suitable unit according to transfusion-service procedures.","Major crossmatch मा agglutination देखिनु परीक्षणमा serologic incompatibility भएको संकेत हो। त्यो unit लाई compatible भनेर issue गर्नु हुँदैन; कारण जाँचेर transfusion-service procedure अनुसार उपयुक्त unit छान्नुपर्छ।","Blood Banking & Compatibility",{status:"reviewed",source:"NCBI Bookshelf — Pretransfusion Testing",url:"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK585033/",basis:"Crossmatch detects antigen–antibody incompatibility through agglutination or haemolysis"}],
  ["A patient is RhD-negative and has a clinically significant anti-D. Which red-cell component is preferred?","बिरामी RhD-negative छ र clinically significant anti-D छ। कुन red-cell component प्राथमिकतामा दिनुपर्छ?",["RhD-positive red cells","RhD-negative red cells","Any RhD type if ABO matches","Washed group AB plasma"],1,"An RhD-negative recipient with anti-D should receive RhD-negative red cells. Component selection must also satisfy ABO compatibility and crossmatch requirements.","Anti-D भएको RhD-negative बिरामीलाई RhD-negative red cells दिनुपर्छ। ABO compatibility र crossmatch को आवश्यकता पनि पूरा हुनुपर्छ।","Blood Banking & Compatibility",{status:"reviewed",source:"Indian National Blood Transfusion Council — Standards for Blood Banks & Blood Transfusion Services",url:"https://cdnbbs.r.s3waas.gov.in/s31177967c7957072da3dc1db4ceb30e7a/uploads/2023/01/2023011812.pdf",basis:"Recommends RhD-negative red cells for RhD-negative recipients"}],
  ["A patient develops chills, fever and back pain during a red-cell transfusion. What is the immediate first action?","Red-cell transfusion चलिरहेको बेला बिरामीलाई जाडो लाग्ने, ज्वरो र ढाड दुख्ने भयो। तुरुन्त पहिलो कदम के हो?",["Slow the transfusion and observe","Stop the transfusion immediately","Give the next unit quickly","Discard the bag without notifying anyone"],1,"Stop the transfusion immediately when a significant acute reaction is suspected. Assess the patient, maintain venous access with 0.9% saline using a new transfusion set, check identification and notify the responsible clinical team and blood bank.","गम्भीर acute reaction शंका भए transfusion तुरुन्त रोक्नुपर्छ। बिरामीको मूल्याङ्कन गर्ने, नयाँ transfusion set प्रयोग गरी 0.9% saline बाट IV access कायम राख्ने, पहिचान जाँच्ने र clinical team तथा blood bank लाई खबर गर्ने।","Blood Banking & Transfusion Reactions",{status:"reviewed",source:"ISBT — Adverse Effects of Transfusion",url:"https://www.isbtweb.org/resources/educational-modules-on-clinical-use-of-blood/adverse-effects-of-transfusion.html",basis:"Immediate reaction management includes stopping transfusion, identity check and maintaining IV access with saline"}],
  ["Acute haemolytic transfusion reaction is suspected. Which laboratory test helps detect antibody-coated red cells in the post-transfusion sample?","Acute haemolytic transfusion reaction शंका छ। Post-transfusion sample मा antibody ले ढाकिएका red cells पत्ता लगाउन कुन test उपयोगी हुन्छ?",["Direct antiglobulin test (DAT)","Bleeding time","Urine pregnancy test","Serum amylase"],0,"The direct antiglobulin test (DAT) detects immunoglobulin and/or complement attached to red cells. In a suspected acute haemolytic reaction, it is performed with repeat blood grouping, antibody screen and crossmatch as part of the investigation.","Direct antiglobulin test (DAT) ले red cells मा टाँसिएको immunoglobulin र/वा complement पत्ता लगाउँछ। Acute haemolytic reaction शंका हुँदा repeat blood grouping, antibody screen र crossmatch सहित यो परीक्षण गरिन्छ।","Blood Banking & Transfusion Reactions",{status:"reviewed",source:"Australian Red Cross Lifeblood — Acute Haemolytic Reactions",url:"https://www.lifeblood.com.au/health-professionals/clinical-practice/adverse-events/acute-haemolytic-reactions",basis:"Lists DAT, repeat grouping, antibody screen and crossmatch in reaction investigation"}],
  ["After a suspected acute transfusion reaction, from where should the post-reaction blood sample ideally be collected?","Transfusion reaction शंका भएपछि post-reaction blood sample आदर्श रूपमा कहाँबाट लिनुपर्छ?",["From the same arm through the transfusion line","From the opposite arm/site, away from the infusion","From the blood bag only","From any unlabeled tube"],1,"Post-reaction patient samples should be collected from a site opposite to the infusion site to reduce contamination with the transfused component. Label and send samples with the implicated component and reaction documentation according to local SOP.","Transfusion भएको ठाउँबाट मिसावट नहोस् भनेर post-reaction बिरामीको sample infusion site को विपरीत हात/स्थानबाट लिनुपर्छ। Local SOP अनुसार सही label, implicated blood component र reaction documentation सहित पठाउनुपर्छ।","Blood Banking & Transfusion Reactions",{status:"reviewed",source:"Australian and New Zealand Society of Blood Transfusion — Guidelines for Transfusion and Immunohaematology Laboratory Practice",url:"https://anzsbt.org.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Guideline_-for_Transfusion_and_Immunohaematology_Laboratory_Practice_FINAL_Published_20210426.pdf",basis:"Specifies immediate post-reaction specimens collected from a site opposite to the infusion site"}],
  ["A patient develops high fever, rigors and hypotension during transfusion. Bacterial contamination is suspected. Which paired investigation is appropriate?","Transfusion को समयमा बिरामीलाई उच्च ज्वरो, कडा कम्पन र hypotension भयो। Bacterial contamination शंका छ। कुन paired investigation उपयुक्त हुन्छ?",["Patient blood cultures and culture of the implicated component","Only stool microscopy","Only serum cholesterol","No cultures are needed if the bag looks normal"],0,"Suspected septic transfusion reaction is an emergency. Obtain patient blood cultures and send the implicated component for urgent Gram stain and culture according to the transfusion-service protocol; begin clinical management promptly.","Septic transfusion reaction शंका हुनु emergency हो। Transfusion-service protocol अनुसार बिरामीको blood culture लिनु र सम्बन्धित component urgent Gram stain तथा culture का लागि पठाउनु पर्छ; clinical management तुरुन्त सुरु गर्नुपर्छ।","Blood Banking & Transfusion Reactions",{status:"reviewed",source:"ISBT — Adverse Effects of Transfusion",url:"https://www.isbtweb.org/resources/educational-modules-on-clinical-use-of-blood/adverse-effects-of-transfusion.html",basis:"For suspected bacterial contamination, recommends patient blood cultures and component Gram stain/culture"}],
  ["A transfusion reaction is reported, but the patient identification on the blood bag does not match the wristband. What is the key laboratory concern?","Transfusion reaction report भयो तर blood bag को patient identification wristband सँग मिलेन। मुख्य laboratory concern के हो?",["Possible wrong-blood-to-patient / identification error","Normal expected variation","Only a platelet-count error","A harmless label colour difference"],0,"A mismatch between patient identification and the component label is a critical clerical warning. Stop the transfusion, verify all identifiers and unit details, notify the blood bank and investigate before any further component is given.","Patient पहिचान र component label नमिल्नु गम्भीर clerical warning हो। Transfusion रोक्ने, सबै identifier र unit विवरण जाँच्ने, blood bank लाई खबर गर्ने र थप component दिनुअघि अनुसन्धान गर्ने।","Blood Banking & Transfusion Reactions",{status:"reviewed",source:"Australian and New Zealand Society of Blood Transfusion — Guidelines for Transfusion and Immunohaematology Laboratory Practice",url:"https://anzsbt.org.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Guideline_-for_Transfusion_and_Immunohaematology_Laboratory_Practice_FINAL_Published_20210426.pdf",basis:"Requires bedside rechecking of patient identity and product compatibility labels"}],
  ["A clinically significant red-cell antibody was previously documented but is now undetectable on the current screen. What is the safest red-cell selection principle?","पहिले clinically significant red-cell antibody document गरिएको थियो तर अहिलेको screen मा भेटिएन। सुरक्षित red-cell छनोटको सिद्धान्त के हो?",["Ignore the historical antibody","Select red cells negative for the corresponding antigen and perform required compatibility testing","Issue any unit without crossmatch","Repeat only the donor's haemoglobin"],1,"A previously documented clinically significant antibody remains important even if it is not currently detectable. Select antigen-negative red cells and perform the required serologic crossmatch in consultation with the transfusion service.","पहिले document भएको clinically significant antibody अहिले detect नभए पनि महत्त्वपूर्ण रहन्छ। सम्बन्धित antigen नभएको red cell छानेर transfusion service सँग समन्वय गरी आवश्यक serologic crossmatch गर्नुपर्छ।","Blood Banking & Compatibility",{status:"reviewed",source:"Guidelines for Transfusion and Immunohaematology Laboratory Practice",url:"https://csbt.org.cn/uploads/soft/210723/3_1715235181.pdf",basis:"Requires antigen-negative red cells for current or historical clinically significant antibodies"}],
["Histopathology: fixation","Fix tissue promptly in an appropriate fixative and use a validated tissue-to-fixative ratio and fixation time. Delayed or inadequate fixation can cause autolysis and poor morphology.","Tissue लाई उपयुक्त fixative मा छिटो राख्नुहोस् र प्रमाणित tissue-to-fixative ratio तथा fixation time पालना गर्नुहोस्। ढिलो वा अपर्याप्त fixation ले autolysis र morphology बिगार्छ।"],
["Tissue processing and embedding","Routine paraffin processing generally includes dehydration, clearing and paraffin infiltration before embedding. Process schedules depend on tissue size and laboratory SOP.","Paraffin processing मा सामान्यतया dehydration, clearing र paraffin infiltration पछि embedding गरिन्छ। समयतालिका tissue को आकार र प्रयोगशालाको SOP अनुसार हुन्छ।"],
["H&E staining","Haematoxylin stains nuclei blue-purple and eosin stains many cytoplasmic and extracellular proteins pink. Staining quality depends on fixation and validated procedure.","Haematoxylin ले nucleus निलो-बैजनी र eosin ले धेरै cytoplasm तथा extracellular protein गुलाबी रंगाउँछ। Fixation र प्रमाणित विधिले staining quality असर गर्छ।"],
["Cytology and FNAC","Cytology examines individual cells and cell groups. Fine-needle aspiration obtains cellular material; adequacy and correct slide preparation are essential.","Cytology मा छुट्टाछुट्टै cell र cell समूह जाँचिन्छ। FNAC ले सुईबाट cell नमुना लिन्छ; पर्याप्त नमुना र सही slide preparation आवश्यक हुन्छ।"],
["Clinical parasitology: stool examination","Fresh stool may be examined directly and by concentration methods according to the suspected parasite. A single negative specimen may not exclude infection.","शंका गरिएको parasite अनुसार ताजा दिसा direct र concentration विधिबाट जाँच्न सकिन्छ। एउटै नमुना negative आउँदैमा संक्रमण पूर्ण रूपमा नकारिँदैन।"],
["Malaria microscopy","Thick films improve parasite detection while thin films help species identification and parasitaemia assessment. Use appropriate staining and quality-controlled microscopy.","Thick film ले parasite पत्ता लगाउन मद्दत गर्छ भने thin film ले species पहिचान र parasitaemia मूल्याङ्कनमा सहयोग गर्छ। उचित staining र QC भएको microscopy प्रयोग गर्नुहोस्।"],
["Blood banking: compatibility","ABO/RhD typing, antibody screening and compatibility testing must follow validated transfusion-service procedures. Resolve discrepancies before routine issue of blood.","ABO/RhD typing, antibody screening र compatibility testing प्रमाणित transfusion-service प्रक्रियाअनुसार गर्नुपर्छ। नियमित रूपमा रगत जारी गर्नुअघि discrepancy समाधान गर्नुपर्छ।"],
["Transfusion reaction investigation","Stop the transfusion when a reaction is suspected and immediately follow the local clinical and laboratory protocol. Check identity, inspect samples and perform indicated tests.","Transfusion reaction शंका भए transfusion रोक्नुहोस् र स्थानीय clinical तथा laboratory protocol तुरुन्त पालना गर्नुहोस्। पहिचान जाँच्नुहोस्, नमुना निरीक्षण गर्नुहोस् र आवश्यक परीक्षण गर्नुहोस्।"],
["Laboratory instrumentation and calibration","Follow manufacturer instructions and laboratory SOP for maintenance, calibration, verification and quality control. Calibration does not replace routine QC.","Maintenance, calibration, verification र QC का लागि निर्माता निर्देशन र प्रयोगशालाको SOP पालना गर्नुहोस्। Calibration ले नियमित QC को स्थान लिँदैन।"],
["Anatomy and physiology: blood and circulation","The heart pumps blood through pulmonary and systemic circuits. Plasma transports dissolved substances; formed elements include red cells, white cells and platelets.","मुटुले pulmonary र systemic circulation मा रगत पम्प गर्छ। Plasma ले घुलित पदार्थ बोक्छ; formed elements मा RBC, WBC र platelet पर्छन्।"],
["Laboratory management and records","Maintain traceable records for specimen receipt, testing, QC, equipment, maintenance, reports and corrective actions according to the quality system.","Quality system अनुसार नमुना प्राप्ति, परीक्षण, QC, उपकरण, maintenance, report र corrective action का traceable अभिलेख राख्नुहोस्।"]
 ];
